message write/read\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.2\",\"AC-2.5\",\"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\",\"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"F-03-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Story 2 thread files are not migrated before message write/read\",\"evidence\":\"Story 3 adds `message` and `message_block` only by changing the version-1 creation migration in `packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts:23-60`. `runMigrations` skips migrations whose version is already current in `packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts:28-31`, and existing thread opens in `runMessageEvents` and `listMessages` call only `openDatabase` (`pipeline.ts:101-104`, `messages/index.ts:89-92`). The accepted Story 2 schema at commit `7c8623d` has `thread_metadata` and `event` tables with `PRAGMA user_version=1` but no message tables. A TSX probe using that schema returned `messageEvents` `{ ok:false, code:\\\"storage_failure\\\", reason:\\\"... no such table: message\\\" }` and `messages.listMessages` `{ ok:false, reason:\\\"... no such table: message_block\\\" }`. That leaves the Story 3 dependency on real Story 2 thread files unsatisfied and blocks AC-2.2/listMessages on an existing valid thread file.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/threads/internal/create.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/storage.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/intake-stream/internal/pipeline.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/messages/internal/store.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.2\",\"AC-2.5\",\"Story 3 dependency: Story 2 real recorded events\",\"Definition of Done: listMessages ordered and deterministic\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.2 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `projectEvent` maps six message-producing kinds to typed blocks, `turn_end` returns null, batch results include `m<eventOrder>`, and `test/projection.test.ts` verifies six messages with full block structures and verbatim content.\",\"AC-2.3 / TC-2.2 on current-schema threads: `turn_end` is recorded in events and absent from messages, verified by `test/projection.test.ts`.\",\"AC-2.4 / TC-2.3: token estimates are stamped via `estimateTokens` in `projectEvent`; identical-content events in two threads produce identical estimates in `test/projection.test.ts`.\",\"AC-2.5 / TC-2.4 on current-schema threads: 300KB+ tool result content reads back byte-identical through SDK and the spawned CLI suite.\",\"AC-2.6 / TC-2.5: actor and harness are copied from event to message and verified unchanged in `test/projection.test.ts`.\",\"AC-5.4 message clause: skipped duplicate events do not reach `createFromEvent`; `test/projection.test.ts` verifies no duplicate message rows.\",\"Projection failure rollback: induced message block failure rejects the batch and read-back remains at baseline.\",\"Configured story gate `green-verify` passed; epic gate `verify-all` passed.\"],\"unverified\":[\"Story 3 dependency / production path for existing Story 2 thread files: no migration is applied before message write/read, and the Story 2 schema probe fails with missing `message`/`message_block` tables.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm --dir /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc exec vitest run test/projection.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm --dir /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc exec vitest run test/cli-process-projection.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --dir /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm --dir /Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"F-03-001: Existing valid Story 2 thread files with `user_version=1` are not migrated before Story 3 message write/read paths, so `messageEvents` and `messages.listMessages` fail with missing-table storage errors.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"Production-path audit found no unallowed fake adapter in the Story 3 message path. Remaining `notImplemented` surfaces are planned future-story surfaces (`messages.list-queued-work`, turns) and outside this story scope.\",\"The projection-failure test seam is explicitly required by the story/tech notes and is exercised through real SQLite rollback state, not a mocked store.\",\"Red-manifest changes rehash the new Story 3 tests and adjust the planned-stub tests after `messages list` became live; the resulting immutability gate passed.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/01-thread-record-and-intake/artifacts/03-message-projection-tokens/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-10T13:57:41.773Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-10T14:03:08.297Z\"}\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:104:### Definition of Done\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/03-readiness-sweep.md:105:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"revise\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"8fc46ccb-e2d5-40ac-ac91-89b3a34c3cb2\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb50e-5338-7942-822f-fd78db817665\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb50e-5338-7942-822f-fd78db817665\",\"storyId\":\"03-turn-composition-chunk-formation\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"03-turn-composition-chunk-formation\",\"title\":\"Story 3: Turn Composition and Chunk Formation\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/001-story-validate.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/compose.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/chunks.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/store.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/derivation.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/scheduler.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/work-queue.test.ts\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Verified Story 3 AC-3.1 through AC-3.9 against the story, tech design, test plan, changed turn/chunk derivation code, provider double behavior, and configured gates. Most turn composition, gap, placement, deterministic chunking, and independent retry mechanics are implemented and covered, but AC-3.8/TC-3.8 lacks the required tool-activity receipt/outcome preservation proof for detailed versus brief chunk summaries.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-3.8-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"TC-3.8 does not prove detailed summaries preserve receipts while brief summaries preserve outcomes only\",\"evidence\":\"Story lines 44-45 require detailed and brief chunk summaries to differ semantically: detailed preserves tool-activity receipts and brief preserves outcomes only. The implemented summary handler in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:126-145 reads only member projections and passes the same { memberProjections } shape to both provider operations. The provider double in packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts:148-153 derives both summaries from the same joined projection text with only the operation marker differing. The TC-3.8 test in packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:481-507 uses a simple prompt/answer turn, asserts only distinct detailed()/brief() marked content, and never creates a tool-run receipt fixture or asserts that detailed carries receipt content while brief strips to outcomes. This leaves a required TC-3.8 assertion unverified.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-3.8-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"TC-3.8 does not prove detailed summaries preserve receipts while brief summaries preserve outcomes only\",\"evidence\":\"Story lines 44-45 require detailed and brief chunk summaries to differ semantically: detailed preserves tool-activity receipts and brief preserves outcomes only. The implemented summary handler in packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts:126-145 reads only member projections and passes the same { memberProjections } shape to both provider operations. The provider double in packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts:148-153 derives both summaries from the same joined projection text with only the operation marker differing. The TC-3.8 test in packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts:481-507 uses a simple prompt/answer turn, asserts only distinct detailed()/brief() marked content, and never creates a tool-run receipt fixture or asserts that detailed carries receipt content while brief strips to outcomes. This leaves a required TC-3.8 assertion unverified.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/turns/internal/derive.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/fixtures/provider-double.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/providers/deterministic.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-3.8\",\"TC-3.8\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-3.1 / TC-3.1: closed turn drains to ready turn_rendering and lower_band_projection independent rows.\",\"AC-3.2 / TC-3.2: failed smoothing falls back to raw prompt, rendering remains ready, and gap records message/form.\",\"AC-3.3 / TC-3.3: repaired smoothing does not mutate the existing gapped rendering; explicit direct requeue rebuilds and clears the gap.\",\"AC-3.4 / TC-3.4: captured composeTurnRendering input carries ordered tool parts with outcomes including the failed call.\",\"AC-3.5 / TC-3.5: turn read-back includes stored chunkId and memberIdx after derivation.\",\"AC-3.6 / TC-3.6: accumulated crossing closes the prior chunk and starts the incoming turn in the next chunk, including threshold equality coverage.\",\"AC-3.7 / TC-3.7: oversized projection self-chunks and closes immediately, including the behind-open-chunk case.\",\"AC-3.8 partial: close queues detailed and brief summary work as separate items with independent states/retry/requeue behavior.\",\"AC-3.9 / TC-3.9: replayed identical event streams produce identical chunk/chunk_member snapshots and summary artifacts.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-3.8 / TC-3.8: detailed summary preserving tool-activity receipts while brief summary preserves outcomes only is not evidenced by code or tests.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm vitest run test/derivation-turns.test.ts\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm exec tsc -p tsconfig.json --noEmit\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"Production summary path currently invokes detailed and brief providers with the same memberProjections-only input; no production code or required test evidence proves the AC-3.8 receipt-versus-outcomes distinction.\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"revise\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"same-session-implementor\",\"openQuestions\":[],\"additionalObservations\":[\"No fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real execution path was found in the audited production turn/chunk derivation path.\",\"Configured story and epic gates both passed, but the blocking AC-3.8 proof gap prevents verifier pass.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T05:01:15.303Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T05:05:18.578Z\"}\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json:1:{\"command\":\"epic-review\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"blocked\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"result\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"canonicalReview\":{\"outcome\":\"block\",\"reviewerLabels\":[\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"epic-reviewer-2\"],\"reconciliationSummary\":\"Both reviewers agree on nearly the whole epic: gates green (independently re-run by this canonical pass: pnpm verify-all exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran), composition discipline structural, read-only enforced at two layers, approved rulings (011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality, 023 strict-read-purity) implemented exactly, no fake or placeholder production paths. The one material disagreement is the health queue section. epic-reviewer-1 treated the listQueuedWork→report-entry-join substitution as a surface-respecting design drift ('arguably stronger for AC-4.5', observation only); epic-reviewer-2 blocked on it with a reproduced divergence (queued:5 vs 4 live work items). Independent verification confirms reviewer-2 on every link: health.ts:92-95 increments queue once per FormReportEntry with a queue join and never calls listQueuedWork; turns/internal/forms.ts:266,296 ('Both turn forms map to the one turn_derivation kind') makes one live turn_derivation work item join onto two form rows (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection); and the shipped test inspect-health.test.ts:174 itself pins queued:5 for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — so the divergence is pinned by the default suite, not edge-case-only. Epic AC-4.5's governing text ('queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail') and the epic NFR ('where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual') are not satisfied as written, no ruling covers the substitution (impl-log rulings 011/011/023 cover other contracts), and the tech design is internally ambiguous (Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as an input yet says 'queue = counts from the live-item joins'). Per the conservative rule, the blocker is retained, not downgraded: EV-04-001 stands as the single blocking finding (absorbing the health half of E04-ER1-002), with human-ruling scope because both fix paths alter a spec'd contract — either count work items from queue detail (breaking the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity TC-4.1 leans on) or ratify form-entry semantics and amend AC-4.5/tech-design wording. Reviewer-1's doc-lag finding (E04-ER1-001) and reviewer-2's (EV-04-002) are the same issue and are merged into one minor finding, fully verified against epic.md:149/156, test-plan.md:38, coverage.md:48, tech-design.md:94 (DD-4 stored-sum wording vs view-report.ts:67 measured tokens), and stories/03-view-contents-report.md ('Spec Deviations: None' despite approved ruling-011). Reviewer-1's remaining observations (overview boundary via pull.meta because ViewStatus at shared/view.ts:128-135 exposes no boundaryPosition; stale stub-era comment at cli/index.ts:473-475) were independently confirmed and retained as non-blocking. No reviewer finding was discarded as unsupported.\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story handoffs completed as tracked: the Story 2 interim view-summary source (pull().meta) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts:121-131), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real composeViewReport — receipt-tracked risks are closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's report(messageId) read (DD-2); one lifecycle script (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8).\",\"Confirmed cross-story semantic drift (the blocker): Flow 4's health.queue counts form-report entries with live queue joins, while Epic 02's queue-detail surfaces (listQueuedWork) count work items — a turn_derivation work item owning both turn forms is counted twice by health (EV-04-001).\",\"Cumulative test baseline never regressed across the four accepted stories (290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests); epic gate re-run for this canonical review: 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS and disposition of every finding; approved rulings are reflected accurately in shipped code — but the health-queue substitution was never the subject of any ruling.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural: domains/inspect imports only other domains' index surfaces, check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/**, and the gate runs it; the domain-graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers per DD-6: every new operation runs under touch suppression, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including the Story 3 storedView field added to the snapshot.\",\"Tech design Flow 4 is internally ambiguous and the ambiguity was resolved silently in code: the flow names listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input and the External Contracts table lists it as 'Used by ... health', yet the same paragraph says 'queue = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins'. health.ts implemented the latter reading and never calls listQueuedWork; no design deviation was recorded and no ruling was sought (feeds EV-04-001).\",\"DD-5 ('overview takes boundary via status') is impossible as written: ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition, so overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta — the only surface exposing it — at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting, but unrecorded in the tech design (E04-ER1-002).\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67, ruling-011 Story 3), sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads, threadId-normalized materialized-file equality with literal pull-output hash equality (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, ruling-011 Story 4).\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, approved); CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers so parity including refusals is structural.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"22 of 23 ACs and 16 of 17 TCs are implemented, traceable, and green: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs across inspect-overview, inspect-view, messages-read, inspect-health, lifecycle, and cli-process-inspect test files; epic gate re-run by this canonical review passed (pnpm verify-all, exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran).\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered as written: TC-4.1's and TC-4.3's shipped assertions (inspect-health.test.ts:63, :174) pin the form-entry semantics — queue equals pending+retrying entry counts — not 'work counts from the owners' queue detail'; on the post-edit cascade the pinned value (queued:5) diverges from the queue-detail work-item count (4).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 ship as threadId-normalized file equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011 (the thread id is the design's one random value; everything else byte-identical, Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal); the relaxation is principled and recorded in the story spec, but epic-level docs still carry the superseded literal wording (EV-04-002).\",\"Zero-provider NFR verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider; the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one.\",\"Closeout items still owed: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded, and the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill exists only as uncommitted working-tree changes (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path: the not_implemented code survives only as vocabulary in shared/errors.ts, the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3, and the lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK through the production registry.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry contains exactly one provider (deterministic — the spec'd v1 state), there is no default provider, and the CLI fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting.\",\"Confirmed material production-path issue (EV-04-001): inspect.health's queue section reports per-form-entry counts, not live work-item counts; on the standard mutation-in-flight cascade it reports queued:5 while the owners' listQueuedWork surfaces hold 4 work items, so the report disagrees with the queue-detail surface an operator would drill into.\",\"Cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still carries the stub-era comment describing 'inspect view' as not-implemented; the route is real and in the help text (E04-ER1-003).\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts are form-entry counts, not the queue-detail work counts AC-4.5 specifies — confirmed divergence, pinned by the shipped tests\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires 'queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail'; tech-design Flow 4 and its External Contracts table name listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input. composeHealth (src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-106) reads only messages.report + turns.report and increments queue once per FormReportEntry carrying a queue join (lines 89-95); it never calls listQueuedWork. The divergence is structural: the turns report join maps BOTH turn forms (turn_rendering, lower_band_projection) to the one turn_derivation work-item kind (src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:266,294-301), so one live turn-derivation item is counted twice. The shipped default suite pins the divergent value: inspect-health.test.ts:174 asserts queue {queued:5, claimed:0} for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — matching epic-reviewer-2's independent reproduction. This violates AC-4.5's source clause and the epic NFR 'where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual', and no approved ruling covers the substitution. Human ruling required because both fix paths alter spec'd contract text: counting work items from queue detail breaks the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity the current TC-4.1 assertion leans on, while ratifying form-entry semantics requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4/External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level artifacts not updated for approved ruling-011 deviations (threadId-normalized file equality; measured loadCost.bandTokens)\",\"evidence\":\"Merged from E04-ER1-001 and EV-04-002; all citations verified. Story 4 ruling-011 (approved) relaxed materialized-file equality to substitute only the random thread id (implemented in lifecycle.test.ts:17-22 and the file-equality assertions), but epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and stories/coverage.md (line 48) still say byte-identical/hash-equal with no qualifier. Story 3 ruling-011 (approved) made loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67), but tech-design.md DD-4 (line 94) still says 'sum of stored band counts', and stories/03-view-contents-report.md's Spec Deviations section still says 'None.' despite that approved public-contract deviation. Code and tests implement the ruled contracts correctly; only the docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design DD-5 not backfilled: overview reads the visibility boundary from pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview composes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) has no boundaryPosition field — overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface exposing it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting and AC-1.1-satisfying, but unrecorded as a design deviation. (The health half of the original finding — the listQueuedWork substitution — is escalated into blocking finding EV-04-001 and not duplicated here.)\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still says the route 'returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed, runInspectView is the real implementation, and the command is in the help text. Comment is false; code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Human ruling required for EV-04-001: decide whether HealthReport.queue counts live work items (per epic AC-4.5's 'work counts from the owners' queue detail' — requires reworking health.ts to consume listQueuedWork and re-stating TC-4.1's consistency clause, since queued+claimed would no longer equal pending+retrying when a turn derivation is in flight) or pending/retrying form entries (per the shipped implementation and tests — requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4 and External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine to ratify the deviation).\",\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log bookkeeping — epic-mandated doc changes that must be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions); not yet written — this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},\"verifierResults\":[{\"resultId\":\"6b026f0b-72fd-4f16-88b6-28f3f56e2b90\",\"outcome\":\"pass\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-1\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\",\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\",\"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\",\"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\",\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\",\"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\",\"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\",\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\",\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\",\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\",\"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\",\"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\",\"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\",\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\",\"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\",\"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-001\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\",\"evidence\":\"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\",\"TC-5.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-002\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\",\"evidence\":\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-1.1\",\"AC-4.5\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false},{\"id\":\"E04-ER1-003\",\"severity\":\"observation\",\"title\":\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\",\"evidence\":\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\"],\"requirementIds\":[],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\",\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"},{\"resultId\":\"7037aa32-e09d-4f0a-b954-6917da95a54b\",\"outcome\":\"block\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"reviewerLabel\":\"epic-reviewer-2\",\"crossStoryFindings\":[\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\",\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\"],\"architectureFindings\":[\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\",\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\"],\"epicCoverageAssessment\":[\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\",\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\"],\"productionPathFindings\":[\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\",\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\"],\"blockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\",\"evidence\":\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-4.5\",\"TC-4.1\",\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true}],\"nonBlockingFindings\":[{\"id\":\"EV-04-002\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"title\":\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\",\"evidence\":\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.3\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-5.3\",\"AC-5.4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":false}],\"unresolvedItems\":[\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\"],\"gateResult\":\"pass\"}]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:43:43.996Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-12T15:54:28.853Z\"}\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/004-verify.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-verify\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"f8c6a343-d37c-4d13-a05d-dea50d12d724\",\"role\":\"story_verifier\",\"provider\":\"codex\",\"model\":\"gpt-5.5\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb775-234f-7dc3-a34a-4b47567a5264\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"codex\",\"sessionId\":\"019eb775-234f-7dc3-a34a-4b47567a5264\",\"storyId\":\"02-smart-compact\"},\"mode\":\"initial\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-smart-compact\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Smart Compact\"},\"artifactsRead\":[\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/test-plan.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/sdk.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-select-golden.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-fixture.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g1-proportions.json\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g2-edge-inclusion.json\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g2-edge-exclusion.json\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g3-oversized-loner.json\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g4-turnless-straggler.json\"],\"reviewScopeSummary\":\"Initial verification covered Story 2 requirements, the full tech-design/test-plan set, compact production code, committed goldens, mapped tests, production-path workaround audit, and both configured gates.\",\"priorFindingStatuses\":[],\"newFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-02-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Selection-rule deviations need a human ruling before acceptance\",\"evidence\":\"The tech design pins the selection walk: smooth stops when an added turn crosses its share except for an empty-band oversized turn, detailed uses the same fill rule, brief fills remaining chunks against its share, and tie-breakers are pinned (tech-design.md:178-185). The story states Spec Deviations: None (02-smart-compact.md:126-128). The implementation adds unresolved interpretations in production code: non chunk-representable banded turns always render in smooth even past share (select.ts:425-463), split chunks retreat from smooth to chunk representation (select.ts:477-495), and brief disables the oversized-loner exception (select.ts:538-542). The implementor artifact lists these as specDeviations/open ambiguity, and g3-oversized-loner.json line 2 commits one of them into the golden. This may be the right product behavior to avoid omission, but current story/design evidence does not authorize it.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g3-oversized-loner.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-2.9\",\"TC-2.2\",\"Selection G1-G4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-02-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Compact receipt lacks an explicit total token count required by AC-2.4\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.4 requires the receipt to report actual per-band and total token counts (02-smart-compact.md:33). CompactReceipt exposes per-band tokens and tailTokens but no explicit total field (shared/view.ts:108-122), and compact returns bands plus tailTokens without a total assembled token count (thread-view/index.ts:395-429). TC-2.2 asserts per-band attribution and tailTokens but does not prove an explicit total is reported (view-compact.test.ts:233-249). The tech-design interface also omits a total field, so this needs either a contract clarification or a small receipt/test update.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"openFindings\":[{\"id\":\"SV-02-001\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Selection-rule deviations need a human ruling before acceptance\",\"evidence\":\"The tech design pins the selection walk: smooth stops when an added turn crosses its share except for an empty-band oversized turn, detailed uses the same fill rule, brief fills remaining chunks against its share, and tie-breakers are pinned (tech-design.md:178-185). The story states Spec Deviations: None (02-smart-compact.md:126-128). The implementation adds unresolved interpretations in production code: non chunk-representable banded turns always render in smooth even past share (select.ts:425-463), split chunks retreat from smooth to chunk representation (select.ts:477-495), and brief disables the oversized-loner exception (select.ts:538-542). The implementor artifact lists these as specDeviations/open ambiguity, and g3-oversized-loner.json line 2 commits one of them into the golden. This may be the right product behavior to avoid omission, but current story/design evidence does not authorize it.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/goldens/g3-oversized-loner.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.5\",\"AC-2.9\",\"TC-2.2\",\"Selection G1-G4\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"blocking\":true},{\"id\":\"SV-02-002\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"title\":\"Compact receipt lacks an explicit total token count required by AC-2.4\",\"evidence\":\"AC-2.4 requires the receipt to report actual per-band and total token counts (02-smart-compact.md:33). CompactReceipt exposes per-band tokens and tailTokens but no explicit total field (shared/view.ts:108-122), and compact returns bands plus tailTokens without a total assembled token count (thread-view/index.ts:395-429). TC-2.2 asserts per-band attribution and tailTokens but does not prove an explicit total is reported (view-compact.test.ts:233-249). The tech-design interface also omits a total field, so this needs either a contract clarification or a small receipt/test update.\",\"affectedFiles\":[\"packages/lhc/src/shared/view.ts\",\"packages/lhc/src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"packages/lhc/test/view-compact.test.ts\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md\",\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md\"],\"requirementIds\":[\"AC-2.4\",\"AC-2.7\",\"TC-2.2\"],\"recommendedFixScope\":\"quick-fix\",\"blocking\":true}],\"requirementCoverage\":{\"verified\":[\"AC-2.1: rg found no production compact invocation outside SDK binding; story tests exercise createSdk().threadView.compact.\",\"AC-2.2/AC-2.3/TC-2.1: built-in profile, explicit field-wise params, invalid sum, non-positive bound, unknown profile, and unchanged-thread assertions are covered in view-compact.test.ts; user profile merge/validation is covered in view-fixture.test.ts and profiles.ts.\",\"AC-2.5/TC-2.3/TC-2.7: degrade ladders, gap entries, derived-only damage success, and canonical state_corruption refusal with prior view intact are covered in render.ts/select.ts and view-compact.test.ts.\",\"AC-2.6/TC-2.4: replaceViewSnapshot uses BEGIN IMMEDIATE delete/insert/boundary reset; crash injection test proves prior view remains and rerun lands clean.\",\"AC-2.7: receipt includes config, per-band entries/tokens, degraded entries, gaps, tailTokens, compactPoint, coveredFrom, and sweep literal absent; explicit total remains open in SV-02-002.\",\"AC-2.10/TC-2.6: band text includes §chunk keys for brief/detailed and §turn keys for smooth, covered by render.ts and view-compact.test.ts.\",\"AC-1.4/TC-1.3: band bytes remain hash-identical across edit and drain of a banded subject.\",\"AC-1.6/TC-1.5: tail deletion disappears from pull; banded deletion leaves snapshot unchanged and status reflects record change.\",\"Architecture-risk tests: restart snapshot durability and coverage edge/no phantom gaps are covered in view-compact.test.ts.\",\"Configured gates: pnpm run green-verify and pnpm run verify-all both passed.\"],\"unverified\":[\"AC-2.4/AC-2.5/AC-2.9 selection semantics remain unverified against the current design until the smooth-obligate, partial-chunk retreat, and brief no-loner interpretations receive a human ruling or are revised.\",\"AC-2.4 explicit total token count remains unverified because no explicit total token count is returned or tested.\"]},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"productionPathFindings\":[],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"needs-human-ruling\",\"recommendedFixScope\":\"human-ruling\",\"openQuestions\":[\"Should Story 2 accept the implementor's selection interpretations (smooth-obligate turns beyond share, partial-chunk retreat, and no brief oversized-loner), or should select.ts/goldens be revised to the literal current tech-design rules?\",\"For AC-2.4, is total token count considered reported when callers can derive it from bands plus tailTokens, or must CompactReceipt expose an explicit totalTokens field?\"],\"additionalObservations\":[\"No material fake adapter, mock path, shim, or placeholder was found in the compact production path. The sweep literal absent and sweep/materialize not-implemented stubs are explicitly allowed by this story/tech design.\",\"Both configured gates passed: green-verify reported 263 tests passed plus test immutability OK; verify-all reported 290 tests passed.\"]},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/004-verify.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T16:12:47.670Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T16:17:15.377Z\"}\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-implement\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"ok\",\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"result\":{\"resultId\":\"b5a6090d-9726-46c7-acec-503f3bfb46db\",\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"model\":\"claude-fable-5\",\"role\":\"story_implementor\",\"sessionId\":\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\",\"continuation\":{\"provider\":\"claude-code\",\"sessionId\":\"8dde17a3-d739-40da-bd65-ee3687cdd63f\",\"storyId\":\"02-smart-compact\"},\"outcome\":\"ready-for-verification\",\"story\":{\"id\":\"02-smart-compact\",\"title\":\"Story 2: Smart Compact\"},\"planSummary\":\"Built compact inside-out per the story's build strategy: (1) render.ts gained the degrade ladders (smooth/detailed/brief resolvers), gap entries as last rung, §subject keys, [degraded: …]/[inter-turn note] markers, and band assembly; (2) select.ts is new — readSelectionInputs (record/forms reads with the canonical-corruption check in the reads, pre-transaction) plus the pure selectArrangement walk implementing rules 1–6 with pinned tie-breakers (≤ inclusion, newest-first, turn-boundary snap, straggler attachment, coverage edge); (3) snapshot.ts gained replaceViewSnapshot — one BEGIN IMMEDIATE doing delete-cascade, header+band insert, and boundary reset; (4) index.ts compact assembles validate → [sweep absent] → read → select → render → injection point → atomic replace → CompactReceipt with sweep: \\\"absent\\\". Entry costs are tokens of the exact rendered entry text (one renderer, no drift). Two ambiguities surfaced during golden derivation and were pinned with code rationale: (a) turns whose chunk straddles the tail or is open are smooth-obligate and always render (AC-2.4's sanctioned over-bound indivisible-entry case — the alternative silently drops spans, violating TC-2.3); (b) a budget stop splitting a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk so it represents whole; (c) the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4's coverage edge is the documented exclusion path). Goldens G1–G4 were hand-derived from the rules against the fixture's deterministic token costs, verified against the pure walk, committed as JSON, and pinned in the immutability manifest.\",\"changedFiles\":[{\"path\":\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/select.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: selection inputs read with pre-transaction corruption detection (CanonicalCorruptionError) + pure six-rule arrangement walk with coverage edge\"},{\"path\":\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/render.ts\",\"reason\":\"Band-entry side: degrade-ladder resolvers per band, gap entries, §keys, degraded/inter-turn-note markers, excerpt lines, band text assembly\"},{\"path\":\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/snapshot.ts\",\"reason\":\"replaceViewSnapshot: atomic BEGIN IMMEDIATE delete-cascade/insert/boundary-reset (AC-2.6)\"},{\"path\":\"src/domains/thread-view/index.ts\",\"reason\":\"compact real: profile/params validation as caller errors, corruption abort, compact-write injection point, receipt with sweep \\\"absent\\\"; stub removed\"},{\"path\":\"src/domains/thread-view/internal/profiles.ts\",\"reason\":\"Extracted profileViolation so construction (throw) and compact (caller-error result) share one rule set\"},{\"path\":\"src/shared/view.ts\",\"reason\":\"CompactReceipt.sweep gains the \\\"absent\\\" literal (Story 3 debt comment referencing this story file); new ViewCompactParams (nested-partial params for field-wise band overrides, AC-2.2)\"},{\"path\":\"src/shared/errors.ts\",\"reason\":\"Two additive caller-error codes: unknown_profile, invalid_view_config (no new classes)\"},{\"path\":\"src/sdk.ts\",\"reason\":\"ThreadViewSurface.compact params type → ViewCompactParams; type re-exported\"},{\"path\":\"test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"Re-recorded: amended view-pull.test.ts, new test files, and the five golden JSONs pinned for immutability\"},{\"path\":\"test/goldens/README.md\",\"reason\":\"Golden inventory, immutability rule, GOLDEN_DUMP=1 regeneration instructions\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 rejections named (105 sum, non-positive bound, unknown profile), thread unchanged by read-back\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1 built-in profile compact, bound+mix in receipt, sweep literal 'absent'\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.1/AC-2.2 field-wise param override over a named profile, receipt profile null\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.2 actuals near shares with whole-entry deviations, zero provider calls, record hash unchanged\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.6 §chunk keys in brief/detailed, §turn keys in smooth\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk coverage edge: covered_from=13, exclusion reported, no phantom gaps\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: architecture-risk restart: fresh SDK pulls byte-identical snapshot\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.4 crash injection at compact-write: prior view serves, rerun lands, no partial rows\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.3 degraded compact: pending rendering → excerpt, failed brief summary → detailed-truncated, c2 gap with reason, full accounting, zero provider calls\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.5 completion leg: status view-health live (degraded=2, gaps=1, builtAt)\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 canonical corruption → state_corruption naming open turns, prior view serves, record unchanged\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-2.7 control: derived-only damage compacts\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.3 banded-subject edit + drain → band bytes hash-identical, rebuilt summary in record only\",\"test/view-compact.test.ts :: TC-1.5 tail delete vanishes; banded delete leaves snapshot; status reflects record change\",\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G1 proportions vs committed JSON\",\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2a exact-fill inclusion (≤ rule)\",\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G2b one-under exclusion, band stops\",\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G3 oversized loner represents alone\",\"test/view-select-golden.test.ts :: G4 straggler rides following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail\"],\"modified\":[\"test/view-pull.test.ts :: sanctioned amendment — compact's not-implemented leg removed (operation is real); sweep/materialize stub assertions kept\"],\"removed\":[],\"totalAfterStory\":263,\"deltaFromPriorBaseline\":20},\"gatesRun\":[{\"command\":\"pnpm run green-verify\",\"result\":\"pass\"},{\"command\":\"pnpm run verify-all\",\"result\":\"pass\"}],\"selfReview\":{\"passesRun\":0,\"findingsFixed\":[\"Initial literal reading of rules 2–4 silently dropped spans when the smooth budget stopped mid-chunk or a chunk straddled the tail (found by dumping the fixture: t4/t5 vanished under 25/25/25/25) — fixed with smooth-obligate always-include + partial-chunk retreat, both grounded in AC-2.4's indivisible-entry over-bound allowance and AC-2.5's never-omit\",\"Compact-point walk had a malformed never-reached-budget branch — rewritten as explicit crossing detection\",\"Referential corruption check wrongly compared chunk members against live turns only — tombstoned turns are legitimate reference targets, now checked against all turn rows\",\"receipt.profile initially named the base profile even when params overrode it — corrected to null whenever explicit params are present (tech design §Storage: 'null when explicit params')\",\"Pinned Partial<ViewProfile> params type could not express the single-band override AC-2.2 itself requires — deepened to ViewCompactParams (nested partial)\"],\"findingsSurfaced\":[\"Golden authoring note: arrangements were hand-derived from the design rules using the fixture's deterministic token costs (dumped via a throwaway script, deleted), then the pure walk was checked against the hand derivation before committing — the goldens encode the rules, with regeneration instructions gated on the deviation process\",\"view-pull.test.ts's skeleton test asserted compact returns not_implemented; amended under the established Epic 02 sanctioned-amendment precedent (cc304bb) and the manifest re-recorded\"]},\"openQuestions\":[\"Default base profile for a bare compact({}) is pinned to 'continuation' (first built-in, the epic's primary PI-continuation user); the design names no default — confirm or change the pin before the CLI (Story 5 surface) exposes it\"],\"specDeviations\":[\"Pinned interpretation (not a behavior change to any stated rule): banded turns with no available chunk representation (chunk open or straddling the tail) always render in the smooth band even past its share — justified by AC-2.4's 'above it (an indivisible turn… included by the selection rules)' and required by AC-2.5/TC-2.3's no-silent-absence; documented in select.ts\",\"Pinned interpretation: a budget stop that splits a fully-banded chunk retreats the included members to the chunk (a chunk represents all of its members or none) — closes the straddle hole rule 3's 'entirely older' would otherwise leave\",\"Pinned interpretation: the brief band has no oversized-loner exception (rule 4 states the coverage edge, not 'same fill rule') — without this, the oldest chunk could never fall outside the window and the coverage-edge AC would be untestable\",\"compact opts params type is ViewCompactParams (nested partial) rather than the sketched Partial<ViewProfile> — AC-2.2's field-wise band override is inexpressible in the sketched type\",\"Additive vocabulary: ErrorCode gains unknown_profile and invalid_view_config (caller_error class; no new classes per the error contract); CompactReceipt.sweep gains the 'absent' literal this story (Story 3 flips it, comment references this story file)\"],\"recommendedNextStep\":\"Run story verification; on acceptance proceed to Story 3 (sweep) — its gate requires confirming the Epic 02 requeue patch and the persisted terminal-failure reason classes (FC-0.4 already proves the fixture side), and it flips the receipt's sweep field from the 'absent' literal to SweepReceipt | { skipped: true }\"},\"errors\":[],\"warnings\":[],\"artifacts\":[{\"kind\":\"result-envelope\",\"path\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json\"}],\"startedAt\":\"2026-06-11T15:11:10.434Z\",\"finishedAt\":\"2026-06-11T16:12:35.367Z\"}\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:1:# Story 0: Foundation\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:54:| `src/shared/view.ts` | the vocabulary types (`ViewProfile`, `VisibilityBudgets`, `SdkViewConfig`, receipts — copy-paste from design §Interface Definitions) |\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:104:### Definition of Done\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/00-foundation.md:105:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/