loseout\\\",\\\"confirmedIssues\\\":[\\\"Residual doc inconsistency (minor, quick-fix): the Flow 2 ASCII diagram in tech-design.md (~line 134) still reads 'loadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }', contradicting the amended DD-4 (~line 94) and the shipped implementation (view-report.ts: bandTokens = measuredTokens(bandMessages), per Story 3 ruling-011). Fix-batch-001 amended DD-4 but missed this diagram line in the same artifact — one-line sweep owed at closeout.\\\",\\\"E04-ER1-002 remainder (observation, deliberately dispositioned): tech-design DD-5 still says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts) exposes no boundaryPosition and overview.ts reads it from pull.meta. Confirmed still present; fix-batch-001 explicitly ruled it out of batch scope as a non-blocking future enhancement, so it carries as a recorded observation, not a closeout blocker.\\\"],\\\"disputedOrUnconfirmedIssues\\\":[\\\"EV-04-001 (prior canonical blocker — health queue counts) no longer stands: the impl-lead ruling recorded in artifacts/epic/fix-batch-001.md RATIFIED form-entry queue semantics, and the spec was amended to match — epic.md AC-4.5 now states per-form-report-entry counts with the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity and explicitly excludes raw listQueuedWork work-item counts; tech-design System View and External Contracts no longer name listQueuedWork as a health input; Flow 4 states the ratified contract citing fix-batch-001; health.ts gained a comment pinning the contract at the count site. git diff confirms health.ts behavior is unchanged (comment-only), as the ruling required, and the previously 'divergent' pinned value (inspect-health.test.ts queued:5) is now contract-conformant. The blocker is downgraded only because the ruling plus amended spec explicitly disprove it as an open defect.\\\",\\\"Fix-run envelope anomaly (bookkeeping, not a code issue): artifacts/fix/001-fix-result.json reports status 'blocked' with PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID (provider stdout was stream-JSON, not the exact result JSON), yet every fix-batch edit is independently verified landed in the working tree. The envelope misreports the batch's substantive outcome; closeout should note this rather than re-run the batch.\\\"],\\\"readinessAssessment\\\":\\\"The epic is ready for closeout. All five fix-batch-001 items independently verify against the working tree: (1) EV-04-001 ratification — epic.md AC-4.5, tech-design System View/External Contracts/Flow 4 amended to the ratified per-form-entry queue contract, health.ts comment added, queue-counting behavior untouched; test-plan TC-4.1's spine ('queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports') is consistent with the ratified semantics. (2) EV-04-002 byte-identical wording — epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2/TC-5.3, test-plan.md TC-5.2, and coverage.md now record the Story 4 ruling-011 threadId-normalized contract. (3) DD-4 reworded to measured pull-served bandTokens, matching view-report.ts. (4) stories/03-view-contents-report.md Spec Deviations now records ruling-011 (measured bandTokens, nullable sourceState). (5) The stale stub-era comment at the 'inspect view' CLI route is removed. git diff confirms all src changes are comment-only — no production behavior changed in the fix batch. Epic gate re-run by this reverify pass: pnpm verify-all PASS, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed. Remaining items are minor: one stale formula line in the Flow 2 diagram (same doc-lag class as EV-04-002, on an artifact the batch touched), the deliberately-out-of-scope DD-5 observation, and closeout bookkeeping — recording the EV-04-001 ratification ruling and the M3/M4 quality-half transfer in the impl log, and committing the working tree (fix-batch doc amendments plus the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill, both still uncommitted). None of these prevent safe closeout.\\\",\\\"recommendedNextStep\\\":\\\"Proceed to epic closeout: (1) sweep the one stale line in tech-design.md's Flow 2 diagram ('bandTokens: Σ stored' → measured per DD-4); (2) record in team-impl-log.md the EV-04-001 ratification ruling (per fix-batch-001), the fix-batch disposition including the invalid 001-fix-result.json envelope (edits verified landed despite the transport failure), and the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic per epic.md Assumptions; (3) commit the working-tree changes — fix-batch doc amendments, comment-only code edits, and the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill in 00-prd.md/01-tech-arch.md — as the epic closeout commit, with the final verify-all PASS (366/366, process suite ran) cited in the closeout record.\\\"},\\\"errors\\\":[],\\\"warnings\\\":[],\\\"artifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"result-envelope\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/002-epic-reverify.json\\\"}],\\\"startedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:03:47.064Z\\\",\\\"finishedAt\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:07:50.516Z\\\"}\\n./packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json:4:    \\\"test/smoke.test.ts\\\": \\\"5d737c488c61457eafa6c672a39e51502da72f9c05ad92339bede702a1da35ec\\\",\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:31:- Story gate: `pnpm run green-verify` — source: explicit CLI flag to preflight; rationale: every story file's §Verification names green-verify as the story gate; the test-immutability guard is compatible because red-manifest regeneration is a sanctioned story step (Story 0 and Story 2 amendments, test-plan §Sanctioned Amendments). Candidates considered: `verify` (skill default when guard exists) vs `green-verify` (spec-pack policy) — spec pack won.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:36:- Pre-epic baseline: Epic 01 suite = 118 tests (per spec pack; verify at Story 0 gate). Expected epic-end ≈ 178–188.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:44:- Ep