sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:123:- run 06:40Z; first implementor attempt lost to runtime silence-timeout interruption (child internally completed but envelope failed; PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE recorded) → resumed 06:56Z; re-implement ~55min; verifier initial PASS, zero findings.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/team-impl-log.md:152:  - **REVERIFY-02-001** — `cascadeTurnDelete` (the third DD-8 caller) now collects each deleted member's live paired counterpart (same-turn members skipped via deleted-read filter + explicit `memberSet`, deduped) into the clear set, exactly as `cascadeFromMessage`/`cascadeMessageDelete`. Cross-turn regression in `epic-fix-02.test.ts`: call in t1, late result in prompt-initiated t2 (summary rebuilt `succeeded`), `deleteTurn(t2)` → m2's call summary cleared/requeued v3, rebuilds `unknown`.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:127:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/03-message-projection-tokens.md:128:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:191:- **TC-4.6** (AC-4.9): Inject a failure at the advance seam (test seam from Story 0); intake a batch that crosses max → intake reports success and all messages committed; boundary unchanged; status read shows the zone sum over max. Clear the injection; intake another batch → the advance lands at target.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:268:**Story 0 — Foundation**\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:284:**Dependencies:** Story 0.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:340:Integration path: Story 1 proves pull on raw threads → Story 2 makes pull serve compacted views → Story 3 makes compacts self-healing → Story 4 makes the tail self-regulating → Story 5 ships the second render. Each story's output is consumed by the next; the fixture from Story 0 carries all of them.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/epic.md:379:- [x] Story breakdown covers all ACs (AC-1.1–1.7, 2.1–2.10, 3.1–3.7, 4.1–4.9, 5.1–5.5) with Story 0 owning foundation criteria only\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:26:| TC-1.2 | Background mode; `delayKind(prompt_smoothing, 50)`; intake batch A; during drain, intake batches B, C | `drainSettled` resolves; all forms ready; scheduler test-hook records exactly 2 passes (initial + one coalesced) |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:91:| TC-6.3 | Delete turn-initiating prompt | Refused `message_initiates_turn`; error names turn id and turns-delete path; nothing changed |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/test-plan.md:104:**Story 0 — versioned work-item ids (DD-1/DD-3).** Ids gain the source-version suffix: `w-t1-turn_derivation` → `w-t1-turn_derivation-v1`. Every exact-id assertion in Epic 01 suites updates accordingly — known sites: `test/work-queue.test.ts` (~8 `workItemId:` literals), `test/cli-process-work-queue.test.ts` (2). Sweep `\\\"w-` literals during Story 0 red phase and list each in the deviation table.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:9:- Story 3 gate verified 2026-06-11 pre-launch (both legs): (1) requeue patch landed — messages.requeue (src/domains/messages/index.ts:284,357) and turns.requeue (src/domains/turns/index.ts:284,383) with already_queued noop, version-scoped idempotent item ids; (2) reason-class persistence — retryable flag flows through work-queue terminal failure path (src/tech-utils/work-queue/index.ts:383-394, scheduler.ts:148-174, handlers); FC-0.4 (passing since Story 0) proves distinguishable transient/permanent classes on read-back via production drains. No Epic 02 patch needed.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:46:- Story Title: Story 0: Foundation\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:156:- Story 3 hard gate (cross-epic): before 03-readiness-sweep starts, verify (1) Epic 02 requeue patch landed (live-work-only queue rows), (2) terminal-failure write path persists a classifiable reason class. If opaque, halt story and surface the named Epic 02 patch (stamp provider `retryable` at exhaustion). FC-0.4 in Story 0 is the fixture-side proof.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/team-impl-log.md:165:5. **storyRunSelection/baseline mismatch.** `validate` reported `baselineBeforeCurrentStory: 365` (workspace-wide test-file count), while the story-lead final package reported baseline 240→255 (lhc package test count). Two different baseline definitions under one name; skill/CLI should pin which one impl-lead compares.\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:112:// ── Story 0 (Epic 02): provider double, shared types, fixture builders ──\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures.test.ts:384:  it(\\\"FC-0.6: the damaged-source thread reads back the corruption it claims (Epic 01 definition)\\\", async () => {\\n./packages/lhc/test/work-execution.test.ts:207:    // …and the burst coalesced: one initial pass plus exactly one follow-up,\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/05-derivation-work-queueing.md:132:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/05-derivation-work-queueing.md:133:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:204:- **AC-4.6**: A derivation whose handler finds source damage (per Epic 01's corruption definitions) lands `blocked` with a reason naming the damage; drain continues past it; re-queue requests for a `blocked` form are refused with that reason.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:253:Delete removes what should not be in the readable record. It is projection-level: the message (or turn) drops from reads and membership while the source events remain in the event log. This is the one sanctioned exception to Epic 01's frozen-membership rule, and an exception for the readable record only — source event membership stays auditable through event read-back, and membership is only ever shrunk, never re-cut. Deleting a message that initiates a turn is refused toward the turn delete: a turn is a prompt and what came back for it, so removing the prompt removes the turn, explicitly, through `turns`. Cascades are bounded by structure: one turn, one chunk; boundaries never move.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:256:2. Validation: target exists, turn closed; message delete additionally checks the target does not initiate a turn\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:267:- **AC-6.3**: Deleting a message that initiates a turn is refused with an error naming the turn and the turn-delete path; nothing changes.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:278:- **TC-6.3** (AC-6.3): Delete a turn-initiating prompt → refused; error names the turn id and turns-delete; full read-back unchanged.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:353:| delete message | `messages` SDK + CLI | message id | exists; turn closed; not turn-initiating | removed id, cleared forms, queued work |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:361:| `message_initiates_turn` | caller_error | message delete targeting a turn-initiating prompt |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:419:### Story 0: Foundation\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/epic.md:425:**Prerequisite:** Story 0\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:25:| Transient classification basis | AC-3.3, epic TD-Q9 | By **reason-code classification table** (per TD-Q9), owned by `sweep.ts`: rate-limit / timeout / provider-unavailable classes ⇒ transient; content-refusal / validation / `unknown_work_kind` ⇒ permanent; **unclassified codes ⇒ permanent** (reported in the receipt as unclassified, never requeued — the conservative default; the other way re-spends on a permanent failure at every compact). Attempt count distinguishes only retrying-vs-exhausted, never repairability. Dependency: exhausted forms must persist the final failure's reason class, not a bare retry-exhausted marker — the Story 0 fixture proves the two failed states carry distinguishable codes; if Epic 02's persisted reason is opaque, that is an Epic 02 patch named at the Story 3 gate. | Resolved — clarified |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:115:Boundary rules, one addition: `thread-view` imports `messages`/`turns` through their `index.ts` surfaces only, never internals; nothing imports `thread-view/internal`; **and `intake-stream` imports the `thread-view` surface** (the advance registration, Flow 4) — sanctioned by the surface-call rule, named here so Story 0's boundary gate expects it. The check-boundaries script gains both lines: thread-view's allowed imports, and intake-stream's added thread-view-surface line. Note for the script: this creates the domain graph's first surface-level cycle (intake → thread-view → messages ← intake) — runtime-safe (registration-then-flush, no import-time execution), but if the script models a DAG it needs a sanctioned-cycle annotation, not a silent pass.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/tech-design.md:295:## Interface Definitions\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:257:**Flows 5/6 — Mutations.** One transaction (`runInTransaction`): validate (exists via deleted-filtered read; turn closed; for message-delete: not turn-initiating — else `message_initiates_turn` naming the turn and the turns-delete path), apply record change (content+blocks+token re-stamp for edit; `deleted_at` stamp for deletes), run cascade (DD-8): bump source version + `pending` on cleared forms, drop forms whose subject is deleted (state rows removed — dropped, not failed, AC-6.6), supersede-delete still-queued old-version items (issue 1), enqueue replacements with target source version, register poke. Claimed old-version items may still finish; DD-3 discards their stale results because their source version no longer matches. Result reports changed/cleared/dropped/queued/superseded. Refusals: `turn_open`, `message_not_found`/`turn_not_found`, second delete of the same id → `message_not_found` by the filtered read (AC-6.7's \\\"refusal, not silent success\\\").\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:395://  message_initiates_turn   caller_error      delete refused toward turns.delete\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:479:| 6 Delete | deleted_at stamps, filtered reads everywhere, initiating-prompt refusal, turn delete, empty chunk | TC-6.1 events-survive-delete; TC-6.5 bounded cascade; TC-6.7 triple-refusal |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/tech-design.md:490:| E02-FIX2 | AC-3.4 spec-compliance restoration (not a deviation) | `composeRenderingInput` groups maximal runs of consecutive tool activity into one `RenderingPart` + one tool-run receipt with an outcome-explicit run account (tools, call count, per-call outcomes; mixed outcomes stay explicit). Per-message mechanical stamping is untouched. | The initial build shimmed one part/receipt per tool message; AC-3.4 and story §Anti-Shim require grouped run accounts. Restores spec compliance. | Done (fix-batch-002) |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:1:# Story 0: Package Foundations\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:74:| Smoke tests | `test/smoke.test.ts`, `test/fixtures.test.ts` (names inferred; Chunk 0 scope) |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:94:| FC-0.3 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | help, unknown command, stub failure shape |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:96:| FC-0.5 | `test/smoke.test.ts` | golden token counts, repeated runs identical |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:129:- Targeted: `pnpm test -- test/smoke.test.ts test/fixtures.test.ts`\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:137:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/00-foundation.md:138:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/01-queue-execution-drain.md:18:- Dispatch through the Story 0 handler map; unknown kind lands `failed_terminal` with stable reason, drain continues\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/01-queue-execution-drain.md:26:**Dependencies:** Story 0 (handler map, migrated queue fields, double, fixtures).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/01-queue-execution-drain.md:164:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/01-queue-execution-drain.md:165:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:66:Strictness falls out of schema construction, not remembered rules: every level (envelope, event, payload) is a closed Effect Schema struct, so unknown-field rejection is a property of the definitions. Server-generated fields are denied by name with their own reason string — the old MVP's silent-root-field-drop bug class gets named when it appears, not just rejected.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:134:- Order counter initializes from `MAX(event_order)` at transaction start; only recorded events increment it.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:146:- Registration/default path: CLI router routes to the real surface, replacing Story 0 stubs; SDK exports the operation.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:159:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/stories/02-event-recording-validation-idempotency.md:160:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:13:**Objective:** The record's removal mutations ship on the cascade machinery Story 5 proved. Message delete drops the message from reads and membership (source event retained), cascades like an edit minus the message's own forms (dropped, not rebuilt). Deleting a turn's initiating prompt is refused with a pointed error naming the turn — `turns.delete` is the operation for that intent, removing the turn and its messages from reads, dropping its forms, shrinking its chunk. Membership only ever shrinks; boundaries never re-cut.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:16:- `messages.delete` (SDK + CLI): closed-turn non-initiating messages; message drops from reads and turn membership; source event remains in event read-back; the message's own forms drop (no rebuild of deleted content); upward cascade re-queues turn + chunk forms (minus-one composition)\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:17:- Prompt protection: deleting a turn's initiating user prompt is refused with an error naming the turn and the right operation (`turns.delete`)\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:35:- **AC-6.3**: Deleting a message that initiates a turn is refused with an error naming the turn and the turn-delete path; nothing changes.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:36:  - **TC-6.3** (AC-6.3): Delete a turn-initiating prompt → refused; error names the turn id and turns-delete; full read-back unchanged.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:55:Delete's cascade differs from edit's in one rule: the deleted subject's own forms **drop** (state rows removed — nothing to rebuild from a deleted source) while everything upward re-queues for minus-one composition. The prompt-protection refusal (`message_initiates_turn`, naming the turn and the turns-delete path) routes whole-exchange intent to `turns.deleteTurn` — a turn is a prompt and what came back for it; no prompt, no turn. Membership only ever shrinks; boundaries never re-cut (the sanctioned exception to Epic 01's frozen membership, and it shrinks in place).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:77:| Storage | `deleted_at` columns (landed in Story 0's migration; first writes here) |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:96:| TC-6.3 | `test/mutations.test.ts` | prompt delete refused `message_initiates_turn`, names turn + turns-delete path |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:153:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/06-message-turn-delete.md:154:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:110:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:162:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:163:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:194:Fixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:283:    mode: \\\"initial\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:334:        - \\\"Definition of Done: SDK exports inspect, CLI routes lhc inspect overview/health, and a focused dist CLI probe verified overview/health JSON equals SDK results.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:335:        - \\\"Production path audit: no material fake adapter, mock path, shim, fallback, or placeholder was found in inspect.overview or inspect.health runtime paths; the inspect.view not_implemented skeleton is explicitly Story 3 scope.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:361:      - \\\"Story 3 explicitly owns threadView.describe, inspect.view, and lhc inspect view; the current inspect.view structured not_implemented result matches the existing surface-skeleton convention and is outside Story 2 readiness.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:402:    planSummary: \\\"Created the inspect domain as a pure surface consumer: shared report shapes in src/shared/inspect.ts; overview composing threads.info + listEvents + listMessages({includeDeleted}) + listTurns/listChunks + both owners' reports + status/pull.meta into the full InspectOverview (absent pieces as zeros/nulls, one composition path, no shape branches); health composing messages.report + turns.report into owner/kind/state counts, failure detail (reason/attempts/lastError from form metadata or queue join), repairPreview (= failed-not-blocked, reported never executed), and queue counts from the same entries' live joins (consistent by construction with pending+retrying). inspect.view ships as the structured not_implemented stub (Story 3). CLI lhc inspect overview|health wired as thin argv-to-SDK wrappers; sdk.ts gains the seam-scoped inspect namespace and shared-type exports. check-boundaries gains inspect's pinned acyclic edge set plus the Epic 04 source check forbidding sqlite/raw-SQL in domains/inspect/**. Fixture extended in place with mutationInFlightVariant (compact + one production edit, drain not settled) and mixedStateVariantThread (ready/failed-transient/failed-permanent/blocked/pending all via intake + scripted provider failures + sanctioned corruption + partial drain). Shared read-only delta helper (observableState/expectReadOnly) lands in test/fixtures and wraps the new ops plus Story 1's list/show retroactively. Smoke-tested the CLI end to end on a fresh thread.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:406:        reason: \\\"New: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport load-bearing shapes (tech design §Interface Definitions)\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:409:        reason: \\\"New inspect surface: overview/health real (touch-suppressed pure reads), view as structured not_implemented stub until Story 3\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:483:        - \\\"threads.info initially returned a state_corruption result under a new error-code semantic for the unreachable lost-metadata-row branch; changed to the existing storageFailure so the story adds no error codes (story contract: 'Error codes: no additions')\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:484:        - \\\"Compacted-overview test initially used default compact (sweep on), which would requeue the transiently-failed form and move the derivation counts; pinned to compact({ sweep: false }) so the two manufactured failed states stay failed and counts assert exactly\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:494:      - \\\"inspect.view stub is routed in the CLI (returns the structured not_implemented result) but deliberately omitted from --help until Story 3 lands the real report.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-003.md:670:State: initialized\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md:74:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md:127:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md:128:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:26:**Dependencies:** Story 1 (drain executes the queued work). Story 0 (double, state types, `tool_call_summary` kind registered).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:151:| 2026-06-11 | Actual sanctioned-amendment edits (the planned tool_call sweep): `test/work-queue.test.ts` restart-survival rows 3→4 (`messageWork` 2→3, list gains `w-m2-tool_call_summary-v1`) + TC-2.9 kind-gate comment; `test/work-execution.test.ts` TC-1.1 (4 items, 5 forms) and maxItems leg (remaining 2→3); `test/cli-process-work.test.ts` TC-1.3 (4 seeded items, 3-row after-kill detail, 5 final forms) — the latter two are Epic 02 Story 0/1 files caught by the same sweep rule. Red manifest regenerated for all three plus the new suite | Implemented; behavior-preserving count/id updates only |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:152:| 2026-06-11 | `test/work-queue.test.ts` handler-map assembly test (Story 0) amended: `expect(sdk.workHandlers).toEqual({})` cannot survive Story 2 registering the real messages table — now asserts exactly the three message kinds and probes the miss with `turn_derivation` (unregistered until Story 3) | Necessary consequence of the story's registration step, not in the pre-listed sweep; flagged for verifier attention |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:155:| 2026-06-11 | `tool_result_summary` forms also carry `metadata.outcome` (stamped from the result's own `isError` via `outcome.ts`) — the epic's tool-activity outcome contract and the Story 0 multi-state fixture already claim this shape; the story text names only the call summary | Additive, consistent with AC-2.4's mechanism |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:156:| 2026-06-11 | \\\"Form read-back on message reads\\\" (Implementation Targets, Surface row) initially deferred to Story 4; verifier finding 02F-001 ruled it in-scope. Implemented: `listMessages` attaches each message's stored `derived_form` rows as `MessageRecord.forms` (one grouped query, stored state verbatim — no read-time derivation; messages with no rows carry no key, preserving AC-2.7). TC-2.1 amended to prove readability through this production path; red manifest regenerated for the suite | Resolved per 02F-001 |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:158:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/02-message-level-derivation.md:159:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:17:| 5 | Registry location and initialization undefined (epic TD question 6) | Resolved | Explicit `registryPath` parameter on registry-touching operations, defaulting to `~/.lhc/registry.sqlite`. Lazy creation on first write; reads against an absent registry return empty list / `thread_not_found` without creating it |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:18:| 6 | AC-1.6 \\\"every thread-scoped operation accepts id or path\\\" is over-broad read literally (`new-thread` has no id yet; `resolve` is id-by-definition) | Resolved — clarified | Thread-scoped means operations on an existing thread's content: `message-events` and all read-backs. Creation and resolution are registry-scoped by nature |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:82:        registry.ts         // registry open/init, row operations\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:118:Import boundaries are enforced from Story 0 by a zero-dependency check script (`scripts/check-boundaries.mjs`, run inside `verify`): no import may reach another domain's `internal/`, and `tech-utils`/`shared` may not import from `domains/`. The ergonomic path for cross-domain calls is the domain's `index.ts` surface, which is also the only path that compiles cleanly under the check.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:151:**Thread creation spans two databases and cannot be one transaction.** Order: create and initialize the thread file first, then insert the registry row; if the row insert fails, delete the file (compensation) and return the error. The invariant \\\"no registry row without its file\\\" holds absolutely (row is written second). The residual crash window — process death between file creation and row insert — leaves an orphan file with no row; it is harmless (nothing references it), detectable (a later registry-refresh feature can adopt or report it), and re-creation at the same path correctly fails `path_exists`, which an operator resolves by deleting the orphan. Documented behavior, not a bug to engineer away at v1 scale.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:181:### 6. Registry location and initialization\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:224:Creation's only interesting problem is that it spans two databases — the new thread file and the registry — and SQLite transactions do not cross files. Design Decision 2 resolves it by ordering plus compensation, and the diagram below is that decision made visible. Resolution and listing are ordinary registry reads; their one subtlety is lazy initialization (Design Decision 6): reads against a registry that has never been written return empty results without creating the database.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:247:The existence check and file creation are not atomic against a concurrent creator racing the same path — accepted under the single-writer assumption (A1); the loser of such a race gets a `system_error` from SQLite rather than silent corruption. Thread-file schema creation runs inside the new file's own transaction, so a half-initialized file cannot result from a crash mid-create: the file either has its full schema and metadata row or fails compensation cleanup, and an orphan from the crash window between the two databases is the documented harmless case.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:257:| TC-1.5 | Listing | Registry scan, lazy-init empty case |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:264:The walk is where most of this epic's behavior lives. Each recorded event takes its order number from a counter initialized at `MAX(event_order)` when the transaction begins — skipped duplicates do not consume numbers, so the stream stays dense and AC-2.1's continuity holds across batches and across skips. Projection happens in the same iteration as recording: the message row, its blocks, the token estimate, and the actor/harness carry are written while the event is in hand, and the message id is the event's order number with an `m` prefix (Design Decision 7), so projection cannot drift from its source.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:340:Strictness is the entire design: every schema is closed (`Schema.Struct` with no index signature, decoded under `onExcessProperty: \\\"error\\\"`), so unknown-field rejection at all three levels falls out of the schema definitions rather than being a rule someone must remember to apply. The decoded result is a typed value the pipeline trusts completely — no defensive re-checking inside the transaction.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:597:**Exit criteria:** `verify-all` passes with zero behavior tests; smoke tests prove the rail (help, unknown command, stub failure shape), fixture validity (builders satisfy the Flow 4 schemas once they exist — initially golden-shaped), tokenizer determinism (golden counts for known strings), and boundary script failure on a deliberate violation (test-only sabotage file, then removed).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:602:**Risk shape:** cross-database compensation; lazy initialization.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/01-thread-record-and-intake/tech-design.md:650:- Story 0 maps to Chunk 0 verbatim; Stories 1–5 map to Chunks 1–5. The epic's story skeletons carry the governing ideas; chunks above add the technical exit criteria.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/coverage.md:26:- **Story 0 fixtures are golden-shaped until consumed.** The multi-state fixture asserts states that only exist for real once Stories 2–4 produce them; the damaged-source fixture is validated against Story 4's blocked path (TC-4.6). Debt: Stories 2/4 confirm the fixtures' claims; Story 0 proves only read-back of what the builders wrote.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/coverage.md:46:- **1:1 flow-to-story mapping plus foundation.** Stories 1–6 own Flows 1–6 exactly as the epic's Recommended Story Breakdown cut them; no AC moved between flows during sharding. Story 0 owns the cross-cutting substrate (provider seam, state types, kinds, migration, fixtures) that the epic's breakdown lists as story 0.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/coverage.md:51:- **Story 0 owns no behavior** and proves the gates (FC-numbered, same pattern as Epic 01's Story 0). Its largest real risk is the migration (FC-0.5: Epic 01 suite green on the migrated schema) — that gate is the story's point.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:89:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:141:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health.md:142:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-thread.ts:1:// The Epic 03 derived-thread fixture (Story 0, FC-0.3/0.4/0.5): one recorded\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment.md:86:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:210), lines 210-242\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment.md:194:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/02-inference-seam-and-model-assignment.md:195:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:20:- Blocked semantics: a handler reading damaged source (per Epic 01's corruption definitions) lands the form `blocked` with a reason naming the damage; the drain continues past it; re-queue requests for a `blocked` form are refused with that reason\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:25:**Dependencies:** Stories 2–3 (real forms in every state to report and repair). Story 0 (damaged-source fixture).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:40:- **AC-4.6**: A derivation whose handler finds source damage (per Epic 01's corruption definitions) lands `blocked` with a reason naming the damage; drain continues past it; re-queue requests for a `blocked` form are refused with that reason.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:151:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/04-derivation-state-report-repair.md:152:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:96:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:272), lines 272-275\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:197:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/06-turn-end-boundary-advance.md:198:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:50:The **source-version check** is the story's architectural heart and TC-5.4 is the epic's named architecture-risk test: a pre-edit item that completes after the edit writes through `forms.ts`'s version check, mismatches, and discards as `stale_discarded` (row deleted, outcome reported) — the post-edit rebuild stands regardless of completion order (AC-5.4). The rule in one line: a background result must not overwrite a derived form if the source changed since the job was queued. The check was built in Story 0, enforced from Story 2's first form write; this story is where it's finally *provoked*. Same machinery serves Story 6's deletes — the cascade module has two callers by design.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:149:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/05-message-edit-cascade.md:150:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:43:  - **TC-4.6** (AC-4.9): Inject a failure at the advance seam (test seam from Story 0); intake a batch that crosses max → intake reports success and all messages committed; boundary unchanged; status read shows the zone sum over max. Clear the injection; intake another batch → the advance lands at target.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:51:The boundary is the view's one self-acting piece — everything else changes by explicit call. Its writers are exactly two: this story's post-commit advance and Story 2's compact reset (already landed; this story proves the reset end-to-end). The advance rides the same `ctx.onCommit` seam as Epic 02's queue poke, registered by intake-stream — which makes this the story that introduces the sanctioned intake→thread-view surface import and the domain graph's first cycle (both pre-cleared in the design and the check-boundaries script per Story 0's DoD).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:98:No host-called advance surface may exist — if a test needs an advance, it intakes a batch (the seam is the only trigger; a test-only `advance()` export would be the forgettable-nudge pattern reborn). The G1 golden's expected positions are hand-derived from the design rules before implementation, same discipline as Story 2's goldens. TC-4.6's injection uses the Story 0 facility's named post-commit point — not a mock of `boundary.ts`.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:112:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/04-tool-result-visibility.md:113:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:110:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151), lines 151-213\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:162:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:163:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:194:Fixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:254:- current_summary: Story orchestration started and durable state has been initialized.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:282:currentSummary: \\\"Story orchestration started and durable state has been initialized.\\\"\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/02-inspect-domain-overview-and-health/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-001.md:336:State: initialized\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures/view-seam.ts:1:// Epic 03 Story 0 view-domain test seams. Lives in fixtures/ — the one\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md:130:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md:131:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:120:Compact through `createSdk().threadView.compact` with real profiles resolved from real `SdkConfig.view`; crash injection through the Story 0 facility's named compact-write point, not a monkeypatch.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:130:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/02-smart-compact.md:131:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:92:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:244), lines 244-270\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:191:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/03-the-adapter-and-the-seven-prompts.md:192:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:1:# Story 0: Foundation\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:21:- Fixture builders: multi-state thread (forms in every state), damaged-source fixture (per Epic 01 corruption definitions), twin SDK/CLI fixtures for parity tests\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:30:Story 0 owns no epic ACs. Its acceptance is foundation criteria, proven by focused invariant tests:\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:45:Story 0 is the tech design's Chunk 0: the substrate every later story dispatches through. Three seams land inert-correct here. The **provider seam** (DD-7) is dependency injection at SDK construction — the deterministic double implements the same `DerivationProvider` interface production adapters will, so tests exercise the production seam, not a mock of internals. The **handler map** (DD-6) is the only join between the queue's opaque kinds and domain code; it assembles at `createSdk` from per-domain `workHandlers` tables. The **enqueue wrapper** (DD-5) makes \\\"queueing is what schedules processing\\\" structural: `enqueue` writes the work row *and* creates-or-resets the form's `pending` state row in the ambient transaction (enqueue is the only place form rows are created — completion is UPDATE-only), and registers the scheduler poke on `ctx.onCommit` — row, state, and poke all commit or all vanish together.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:102:| Enqueue atomicity | `test/work-queue.test.ts` | induced rollback after `enqueue` → no work row, no `pending` form row, no poke fired | Story 0 owns no epic TCs; this invariant underlies every later queue site |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:137:**Cross-story debt** (coverage.md): the multi-state and damaged-source fixtures are golden-shaped until consumed — Story 0 proves read-back of what the builders wrote; Stories 2/4 confirm the states arise for real.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:163:| 2026-06-10 | Work-item ids gain the version suffix (`w-<sourceId>-<kind>-v<sourceVersion>`), changing Epic 01 exact-id assertions — sanctioned amendment, see test plan §Sanctioned Amendments (Story 0 entry); red manifest regenerates as a story step | Planned amendment; record actual edits here during implementation |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:165:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/00-foundation.md:166:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:70:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md:189), lines 189-213\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:120:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/stories/01-message-read-surface.md:121:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/coverage.md:50:TC ownership count: Story 1 owns TC-1.1, TC-1.2, TC-1.4, TC-2.5 (4); Story 2 owns TC-1.3, TC-1.5, TC-2.1, TC-2.2, TC-2.3, TC-2.4, TC-2.6, TC-2.7 (8); Story 3 owns TC-3.1–TC-3.4 (4); Story 4 owns TC-4.1–TC-4.6 (6); Story 5 owns TC-5.1–TC-5.5 (5). Total 27/27. Story 0 owns FC-0.1–0.6 only.\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:4:// and handlers land in Stories 1–3) — Story 0 proves read-back of what the\\n./packages/lhc/test/fixtures/threads.ts:301:// ── damaged-source thread (Epic 01 corruption definition) ────────\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md:25:**Dependencies:** Story 2 (message forms to compose from). Story 1 (drain). Story 0 (double's compose/project/summarize operations, chunk kinds registered).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md:149:- **Tool-run grouping (Fix 2, fix-batch-002) — spec-compliance restoration, not a deviation.** `composeRenderingInput` folds maximal runs of consecutive tool activity into one `RenderingPart` and one tool-run receipt, each carrying an outcome-explicit run account (tools used, call count, per-call mechanical outcomes; mixed outcomes stay explicit, never collapsed into a vague success), as AC-3.4 and §Anti-Shim Requirements require. The initial build shimmed one part/receipt per tool message; this restores the grouped-run contract. Per-message mechanical stamping (AC-2.4) is untouched; gaps stay per-message.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md:152:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/stories/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation.md:153:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:80:- [tech-design.md §Interface Definitions](/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:252), lines 252-258\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:160:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/04-failure-classification.md:161:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:15:- `thread-view` surface skeleton (structured-result stubs per tech design §Interface Definitions) with `pull` and `status` implemented\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:21:**Dependencies:** Story 0 (fixture, migration, profiles).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:46:Types first (`shared/view.ts` landed in Story 0 — consume, don't redefine), then the surface skeleton with all five stubs (Red asserts each returns `{ ok: false, reason: \\\"not implemented: <op>\\\" }`), then Green: `render.ts` tail formatting kind-by-kind against the mapping table, then `pull` assembly, then `status`. The mapping table is seven rows — implement and test them as seven legs, not one blob assertion, so a single kind's drift fails one named test.\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:75:| TC-1.4 | `view-pull.test.ts` | boundary seeded mid-tail (Story 0 helper): short behind, full ahead, prompts/text full everywhere |\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:92:All reads through the real SDK surface (`createSdk().threadView.pull/status`) against real temp thread files from the Story 0 fixture. No internal-function shortcuts in TC tests (golden/unit tests of `render.ts` legs may call internals; the TC rows go through the surface).\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:102:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/01-pull-and-status.md:103:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/tech-design.md:151:## Interface Definitions\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:180:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/stories/05-real-inference-suite-and-capstone.md:181:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"init\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"tools\\\":[\\\"Task\\\",\\\"AskUserQuestion\\\",\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"CronCreate\\\",\\\"CronDelete\\\",\\\"CronList\\\",\\\"DesignSync\\\",\\\"Edit\\\",\\\"EnterPlanMode\\\",\\\"EnterWorktree\\\",\\\"ExitPlanMode\\\",\\\"ExitWorktree\\\",\\\"Monitor\\\",\\\"NotebookEdit\\\",\\\"PushNotification\\\",\\\"Read\\\",\\\"RemoteTrigger\\\",\\\"ScheduleWakeup\\\",\\\"Skill\\\",\\\"TaskCreate\\\",\\\"TaskGet\\\",\\\"TaskList\\\",\\\"TaskOutput\\\",\\\"TaskStop\\\",\\\"TaskUpdate\\\",\\\"ToolSearch\\\",\\\"WebFetch\\\",\\\"WebSearch\\\",\\\"Workflow\\\",\\\"Write\\\"],\\\"mcp_servers\\\":[],\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-fable-5\\\",\\\"permissionMode\\\":\\\"bypassPermissions\\\",\\\"slash_commands\\\":[\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"design-sync\\\",\\\"update-config\\\",\\\"verify\\\",\\\"debug\\\",\\\"code-review\\\",\\\"simplify\\\",\\\"batch\\\",\\\"fewer-permission-prompts\\\",\\\"loop\\\",\\\"schedule\\\",\\\"claude-api\\\",\\\"run\\\",\\\"run-skill-generator\\\",\\\"clear\\\",\\\"compact\\\",\\\"context\\\",\\\"heapdump\\\",\\\"init\\\",\\\"reload-skills\\\",\\\"review\\\",\\\"security-review\\\",\\\"usage-credits\\\",\\\"extra-usage\\\",\\\"usage\\\",\\\"insights\\\",\\\"goal\\\",\\\"team-onboarding\\\"],\\\"apiKeySource\\\":\\\"none\\\",\\\"claude_code_version\\\":\\\"2.1.175\\\",\\\"output_style\\\":\\\"default\\\",\\\"agents\\\":[\\\"claude\\\",\\\"Explore\\\",\\\"general-purpose\\\",\\\"Plan\\\",\\\"statusline-setup\\\"],\\\"skills\\\":[\\\"deep-research\\\",\\\"design-sync\\\",\\\"update-config\\\",\\\"verify\\\",\\\"debug\\\",\\\"code-review\\\",\\\"simplify\\\",\\\"batch\\\",\\\"fewer-permission-prompts\\\",\\\"loop\\\",\\\"schedule\\\",\\\"claude-api\\\",\\\"run\\\",\\\"run-skill-generator\\\"],\\\"plugins\\\":[],\\\"analytics_disabled\\\":false,\\\"product_feedback_disabled\\\":false,\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"9fb3384e-afe9-4f46-98c1-5b9ba592abbc\\\",\\\"memory_paths\\\":{\\\"auto\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/.claude/projects/-Users-leemoore-code-pi-long-horizon-liminal-context/memory/\\\"},\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\"}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:31:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01GiVtLqABvhqfqwupkLkzf8\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-review\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"canonicalReview\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabels\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"reconciliationSummary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Both reviewers agree on nearly the whole epic: gates green (independently re-run by this canonical pass: pnpm verify-all exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran), composition discipline structural, read-only enforced at two layers, approved rulings (011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality, 023 strict-read-purity) implemented exactly, no fake or placeholder production paths. The one material disagreement is the health queue section. epic-reviewer-1 treated the listQueuedWork→report-entry-join substitution as a surface-respecting design drift ('arguably stronger for AC-4.5', observation only); epic-reviewer-2 blocked on it with a reproduced divergence (queued:5 vs 4 live work items). Independent verification confirms reviewer-2 on every link: health.ts:92-95 increments queue once per FormReportEntry with a queue join and never calls listQueuedWork; turns/internal/forms.ts:266,296 ('Both turn forms map to the one turn_derivation kind') makes one live turn_derivation work item join onto two form rows (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection); and the shipped test inspect-health.test.ts:174 itself pins queued:5 for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — so the divergence is pinned by the default suite, not edge-case-only. Epic AC-4.5's governing text ('queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail') and the epic NFR ('where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual') are not satisfied as written, no ruling covers the substitution (impl-log rulings 011/011/023 cover other contracts), and the tech design is internally ambiguous (Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as an input yet says 'queue = counts from the live-item joins'). Per the conservative rule, the blocker is retained, not downgraded: EV-04-001 stands as the single blocking finding (absorbing the health half of E04-ER1-002), with human-ruling scope because both fix paths alter a spec'd contract — either count work items from queue detail (breaking the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity TC-4.1 leans on) or ratify form-entry semantics and amend AC-4.5/tech-design wording. Reviewer-1's doc-lag finding (E04-ER1-001) and reviewer-2's (EV-04-002) are the same issue and are merged into one minor finding, fully verified against epic.md:149/156, test-plan.md:38, coverage.md:48, tech-design.md:94 (DD-4 stored-sum wording vs view-report.ts:67 measured tokens), and stories/03-view-contents-report.md ('Spec Deviations: None' despite approved ruling-011). Reviewer-1's remaining observations (overview boundary via pull.meta because ViewStatus at shared/view.ts:128-135 exposes no boundaryPosition; stale stub-era comment at cli/index.ts:473-475) were independently confirmed and retained as non-blocking. No reviewer finding was discarded as unsupported.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Story handoffs completed as tracked: the Story 2 interim view-summary source (pull().meta) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts:121-131), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real composeViewReport — receipt-tracked risks are closed in code, not just in the log.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's report(messageId) read (DD-2); one lifecycle script (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Confirmed cross-story semantic drift (the blocker): Flow 4's health.queue counts form-report entries with live queue joins, while Epic 02's queue-detail surfaces (listQueuedWork) count work items — a turn_derivation work item owning both turn forms is counted twice by health (EV-04-001).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cumulative test baseline never regressed across the four accepted stories (290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests); epic gate re-run for this canonical review: 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS and disposition of every finding; approved rulings are reflected accurately in shipped code — but the health-queue substitution was never the subject of any ruling.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Composition discipline is structural: domains/inspect imports only other domains' index surfaces, check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/**, and the gate runs it; the domain-graph addition is acyclic as designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Read-only is enforced at two layers per DD-6: every new operation runs under touch suppression, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including the Story 3 storedView field added to the snapshot.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Tech design Flow 4 is internally ambiguous and the ambiguity was resolved silently in code: the flow names listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input and the External Contracts table lists it as 'Used by ... health', yet the same paragraph says 'queue = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins'. health.ts implemented the latter reading and never calls listQueuedWork; no design deviation was recorded and no ruling was sought (feeds EV-04-001).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"DD-5 ('overview takes boundary via status') is impossible as written: ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition, so overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta — the only surface exposing it — at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting, but unrecorded in the tech design (E04-ER1-002).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67, ruling-011 Story 3), sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads, threadId-normalized materialized-file equality with literal pull-output hash equality (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, ruling-011 Story 4).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, approved); CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers so parity including refusals is structural.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"22 of 23 ACs and 16 of 17 TCs are implemented, traceable, and green: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs across inspect-overview, inspect-view, messages-read, inspect-health, lifecycle, and cli-process-inspect test files; epic gate re-run by this canonical review passed (pnpm verify-all, exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered as written: TC-4.1's and TC-4.3's shipped assertions (inspect-health.test.ts:63, :174) pin the form-entry semantics — queue equals pending+retrying entry counts — not 'work counts from the owners' queue detail'; on the post-edit cascade the pinned value (queued:5) diverges from the queue-detail work-item count (4).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 ship as threadId-normalized file equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011 (the thread id is the design's one random value; everything else byte-identical, Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal); the relaxation is principled and recorded in the story spec, but epic-level docs still carry the superseded literal wording (EV-04-002).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Zero-provider NFR verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider; the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Closeout items still owed: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded, and the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill exists only as uncommitted working-tree changes (see unresolvedItems).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path: the not_implemented code survives only as vocabulary in shared/errors.ts, the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3, and the lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK through the production registry.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry contains exactly one provider (deterministic — the spec'd v1 state), there is no default provider, and the CLI fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Confirmed material production-path issue (EV-04-001): inspect.health's queue section reports per-form-entry counts, not live work-item counts; on the standard mutation-in-flight cascade it reports queued:5 while the owners' listQueuedWork surfaces hold 4 work items, so the report disagrees with the queue-detail surface an operator would drill into.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still carries the stub-era comment describing 'inspect view' as not-implemented; the route is real and in the help text (E04-ER1-003).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Health queue counts are form-entry counts, not the queue-detail work counts AC-4.5 specifies — confirmed divergence, pinned by the shipped tests\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic AC-4.5 requires 'queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail'; tech-design Flow 4 and its External Contracts table name listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input. composeHealth (src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-106) reads only messages.report + turns.report and increments queue once per FormReportEntry carrying a queue join (lines 89-95); it never calls listQueuedWork. The divergence is structural: the turns report join maps BOTH turn forms (turn_rendering, lower_band_projection) to the one turn_derivation work-item kind (src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:266,294-301), so one live turn-derivation item is counted twice. The shipped default suite pins the divergent value: inspect-health.test.ts:174 asserts queue {queued:5, claimed:0} for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — matching epic-reviewer-2's independent reproduction. This violates AC-4.5's source clause and the epic NFR 'where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual', and no approved ruling covers the substitution. Human ruling required because both fix paths alter spec'd contract text: counting work items from queue detail breaks the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity the current TC-4.1 assertion leans on, while ratifying form-entry semantics requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4/External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-4.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic-level artifacts not updated for approved ruling-011 deviations (threadId-normalized file equality; measured loadCost.bandTokens)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Merged from E04-ER1-001 and EV-04-002; all citations verified. Story 4 ruling-011 (approved) relaxed materialized-file equality to substitute only the random thread id (implemented in lifecycle.test.ts:17-22 and the file-equality assertions), but epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and stories/coverage.md (line 48) still say byte-identical/hash-equal with no qualifier. Story 3 ruling-011 (approved) made loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67), but tech-design.md DD-4 (line 94) still says 'sum of stored band counts', and stories/03-view-contents-report.md's Spec Deviations section still says 'None.' despite that approved public-contract deviation. Code and tests implement the ruled contracts correctly; only the docs lag.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-5.2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Tech design DD-5 not backfilled: overview reads the visibility boundary from pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview composes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) has no boundaryPosition field — overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface exposing it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting and AC-1.1-satisfying, but unrecorded as a design deviation. (The health half of the original finding — the listQueuedWork substitution — is escalated into blocking finding EV-04-001 and not duplicated here.)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still says the route 'returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed, runInspectView is the real implementation, and the command is in the help text. Comment is false; code is correct.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Human ruling required for EV-04-001: decide whether HealthReport.queue counts live work items (per epic AC-4.5's 'work counts from the owners' queue detail' — requires reworking health.ts to consume listQueuedWork and re-stating TC-4.1's consistency clause, since queued+claimed would no longer equal pending+retrying when a turn derivation is in flight) or pending/retrying form entries (per the shipped implementation and tests — requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4 and External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine to ratify the deviation).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log bookkeeping — epic-mandated doc changes that must be committed as part of epic closeout.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions); not yet written — this review is upstream of that closeout step.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"verifierResults\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"resultId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"6b026f0b-72fd-4f16-88b6-28f3f56e2b90\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-fable-5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-5.2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"resultId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"7037aa32-e09d-4f0a-b954-6917da95a54b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"gpt-5.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-4.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"artifacts\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"result-envelope\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"startedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:43:43.996Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finishedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:54:28.853Z\\\\\\\"}\\\\n2\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"424e2f32-086e-4dfc-9d55-76643b377be1\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:04:02.490Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-review\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"result\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"canonicalReview\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabels\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"reconciliationSummary\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Both reviewers agree on nearly the whole epic: gates green (independently re-run by this canonical pass: pnpm verify-all exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran), composition discipline structural, read-only enforced at two layers, approved rulings (011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality, 023 strict-read-purity) implemented exactly, no fake or placeholder production paths. The one material disagreement is the health queue section. epic-reviewer-1 treated the listQueuedWork→report-entry-join substitution as a surface-respecting design drift ('arguably stronger for AC-4.5', observation only); epic-reviewer-2 blocked on it with a reproduced divergence (queued:5 vs 4 live work items). Independent verification confirms reviewer-2 on every link: health.ts:92-95 increments queue once per FormReportEntry with a queue join and never calls listQueuedWork; turns/internal/forms.ts:266,296 ('Both turn forms map to the one turn_derivation kind') makes one live turn_derivation work item join onto two form rows (turn_rendering + lower_band_projection); and the shipped test inspect-health.test.ts:174 itself pins queued:5 for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — so the divergence is pinned by the default suite, not edge-case-only. Epic AC-4.5's governing text ('queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail') and the epic NFR ('where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual') are not satisfied as written, no ruling covers the substitution (impl-log rulings 011/011/023 cover other contracts), and the tech design is internally ambiguous (Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as an input yet says 'queue = counts from the live-item joins'). Per the conservative rule, the blocker is retained, not downgraded: EV-04-001 stands as the single blocking finding (absorbing the health half of E04-ER1-002), with human-ruling scope because both fix paths alter a spec'd contract — either count work items from queue detail (breaking the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity TC-4.1 leans on) or ratify form-entry semantics and amend AC-4.5/tech-design wording. Reviewer-1's doc-lag finding (E04-ER1-001) and reviewer-2's (EV-04-002) are the same issue and are merged into one minor finding, fully verified against epic.md:149/156, test-plan.md:38, coverage.md:48, tech-design.md:94 (DD-4 stored-sum wording vs view-report.ts:67 measured tokens), and stories/03-view-contents-report.md ('Spec Deviations: None' despite approved ruling-011). Reviewer-1's remaining observations (overview boundary via pull.meta because ViewStatus at shared/view.ts:128-135 exposes no boundaryPosition; stale stub-era comment at cli/index.ts:473-475) were independently confirmed and retained as non-blocking. No reviewer finding was discarded as unsupported.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Story handoffs completed as tracked: the Story 2 interim view-summary source (pull().meta) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts:121-131), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real composeViewReport — receipt-tracked risks are closed in code, not just in the log.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's report(messageId) read (DD-2); one lifecycle script (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) drives all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Confirmed cross-story semantic drift (the blocker): Flow 4's health.queue counts form-report entries with live queue joins, while Epic 02's queue-detail surfaces (listQueuedWork) count work items — a turn_derivation work item owning both turn forms is counted twice by health (EV-04-001).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cumulative test baseline never regressed across the four accepted stories (290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests); epic gate re-run for this canonical review: 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS and disposition of every finding; approved rulings are reflected accurately in shipped code — but the health-queue substitution was never the subject of any ruling.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Composition discipline is structural: domains/inspect imports only other domains' index surfaces, check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/**, and the gate runs it; the domain-graph addition is acyclic as designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Read-only is enforced at two layers per DD-6: every new operation runs under touch suppression, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including the Story 3 storedView field added to the snapshot.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Tech design Flow 4 is internally ambiguous and the ambiguity was resolved silently in code: the flow names listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input and the External Contracts table lists it as 'Used by ... health', yet the same paragraph says 'queue = queued/claimed counts from the live-item joins'. health.ts implemented the latter reading and never calls listQueuedWork; no design deviation was recorded and no ruling was sought (feeds EV-04-001).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"DD-5 ('overview takes boundary via status') is impossible as written: ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition, so overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta — the only surface exposing it — at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting, but unrecorded in the tech design (E04-ER1-002).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67, ruling-011 Story 3), sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads, threadId-normalized materialized-file equality with literal pull-output hash equality (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, ruling-011 Story 4).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, approved); CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers so parity including refusals is structural.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"22 of 23 ACs and 16 of 17 TCs are implemented, traceable, and green: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs across inspect-overview, inspect-view, messages-read, inspect-health, lifecycle, and cli-process-inspect test files; epic gate re-run by this canonical review passed (pnpm verify-all, exit 0, 366/366 tests, 44 files, process suite ran).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered as written: TC-4.1's and TC-4.3's shipped assertions (inspect-health.test.ts:63, :174) pin the form-entry semantics — queue equals pending+retrying entry counts — not 'work counts from the owners' queue detail'; on the post-edit cascade the pinned value (queued:5) diverges from the queue-detail work-item count (4).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 ship as threadId-normalized file equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011 (the thread id is the design's one random value; everything else byte-identical, Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal); the relaxation is principled and recorded in the story spec, but epic-level docs still carry the superseded literal wording (EV-04-002).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Zero-provider NFR verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider; the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Closeout items still owed: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded, and the sanctioned PRD/tech-arch search-deferral backfill exists only as uncommitted working-tree changes (see unresolvedItems).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path: the not_implemented code survives only as vocabulary in shared/errors.ts, the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3, and the lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK through the production registry.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry contains exactly one provider (deterministic — the spec'd v1 state), there is no default provider, and the CLI fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Confirmed material production-path issue (EV-04-001): inspect.health's queue section reports per-form-entry counts, not live work-item counts; on the standard mutation-in-flight cascade it reports queued:5 while the owners' listQueuedWork surfaces hold 4 work items, so the report disagrees with the queue-detail surface an operator would drill into.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still carries the stub-era comment describing 'inspect view' as not-implemented; the route is real and in the help text (E04-ER1-003).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Health queue counts are form-entry counts, not the queue-detail work counts AC-4.5 specifies — confirmed divergence, pinned by the shipped tests\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic AC-4.5 requires 'queued and claimed work counts from the owners' queue detail'; tech-design Flow 4 and its External Contracts table name listQueuedWork (both owners) as a health input. composeHealth (src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-106) reads only messages.report + turns.report and increments queue once per FormReportEntry carrying a queue join (lines 89-95); it never calls listQueuedWork. The divergence is structural: the turns report join maps BOTH turn forms (turn_rendering, lower_band_projection) to the one turn_derivation work-item kind (src/domains/turns/internal/forms.ts:266,294-301), so one live turn-derivation item is counted twice. The shipped default suite pins the divergent value: inspect-health.test.ts:174 asserts queue {queued:5, claimed:0} for the post-edit cascade whose owners' queue detail holds exactly 4 work items (prompt_smoothing, turn_derivation, chunk_summary_brief, chunk_summary_detailed) — matching epic-reviewer-2's independent reproduction. This violates AC-4.5's source clause and the epic NFR 'where a report describes another surface's output ... equality is contractual', and no approved ruling covers the substitution. Human ruling required because both fix paths alter spec'd contract text: counting work items from queue detail breaks the queued+claimed = pending+retrying identity the current TC-4.1 assertion leans on, while ratifying form-entry semantics requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4/External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-4.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic-level artifacts not updated for approved ruling-011 deviations (threadId-normalized file equality; measured loadCost.bandTokens)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Merged from E04-ER1-001 and EV-04-002; all citations verified. Story 4 ruling-011 (approved) relaxed materialized-file equality to substitute only the random thread id (implemented in lifecycle.test.ts:17-22 and the file-equality assertions), but epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and stories/coverage.md (line 48) still say byte-identical/hash-equal with no qualifier. Story 3 ruling-011 (approved) made loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages (view-report.ts:67), but tech-design.md DD-4 (line 94) still says 'sum of stored band counts', and stories/03-view-contents-report.md's Spec Deviations section still says 'None.' despite that approved public-contract deviation. Code and tests implement the ruled contracts correctly; only the docs lag.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-5.2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Tech design DD-5 not backfilled: overview reads the visibility boundary from pull.meta because ViewStatus exposes no boundaryPosition\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview composes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) has no boundaryPosition field — overview.ts:121-128 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface exposing it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Surface-respecting and AC-1.1-satisfying, but unrecorded as a design deviation. (The health half of the original finding — the listQueuedWork substitution — is escalated into blocking finding EV-04-001 and not duplicated here.)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still says the route 'returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed, runInspectView is the real implementation, and the command is in the help text. Comment is false; code is correct.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Human ruling required for EV-04-001: decide whether HealthReport.queue counts live work items (per epic AC-4.5's 'work counts from the owners' queue detail' — requires reworking health.ts to consume listQueuedWork and re-stating TC-4.1's consistency clause, since queued+claimed would no longer equal pending+retrying when a turn derivation is in flight) or pending/retrying form entries (per the shipped implementation and tests — requires amending AC-4.5, tech-design Flow 4 and External Contracts, and the test-plan TC-4.1 spine to ratify the deviation).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log bookkeeping — epic-mandated doc changes that must be committed as part of epic closeout.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions); not yet written — this review is upstream of that closeout step.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},\\\\\\\"verifierResults\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"resultId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"6b026f0b-72fd-4f16-88b6-28f3f56e2b90\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-code\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"claude-fable-5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Story 2 → Story 3 handoff completed as tracked: overview's interim view-summary source (pull().meta, Story 2 approved deviation) was swapped to threadView.describe in Story 3 (overview.ts), and the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced with the real composeViewReport. The receipt-tracked risk is closed in code, not just in the log.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Shared vocabulary discipline holds across stories: report shapes live in src/shared/inspect.ts (Story 2) and Story 3 consumes them without redefinition; messages.show reuses the owner's reportMessageForms read (DD-2) rather than new join machinery; the lifecycle fixture (test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts) is one script driven by all four TC-5 legs including the process-suite leg (DD-8), so replay/teardown/CLI runs exercise the same sequence.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"The read-only delta helper (test/fixtures/read-only-delta.ts, Story 2) wraps Story 1's ops retroactively as the test plan required: inspect-overview/view/health tests use expectReadOnly, messages-read uses the same observableState snapshot directly, and the Story 3 storedView field was added to the snapshot so a forgotten view touch is caught even when pull meta would not show it.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Cumulative baseline never regressed: 290 → 300 → 313 → 320 → 328 default tests across the four accepted stories; epic gate run for this review shows 366 tests / 44 files with the process suite included.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"All four story receipts in team-impl-log.md show accepted status with verifier PASS, impl-lead-run gates, and disposition of every finding (SV-01-001..005, SV-03-001, SV-04-001); approved rulings (023 strict-read-purity, 011 Story 3 loadCost/sourceState, 011 Story 4 threadId-normalized file equality) are all reflected accurately in the shipped code.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Composition discipline is structural, not aspirational: domains/inspect imports only the five other domains' index surfaces (verified in source), check-boundaries.mjs carries the inspect dependency allowlist plus the Epic 04 source check rejecting raw storage access from domains/inspect/** (scripts/check-boundaries.mjs:77-115), and the gate runs it. The domain graph addition is acyclic as designed.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Read-only is enforced at two layers as DD-6 demanded: every new operation (inspect.overview/view/health, threadView.describe, messages.listMessages/show) runs under runWithThreadTouchSuppressed so a background scheduler can never hang a catch-up drain off a read, and tests assert absence-of-delta over observable state including raw derived_form rows.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Minor drift from tech-design mechanics, surface-respecting in both cases: (1) DD-5 says overview takes boundary 'via status' but ViewStatus does not expose boundaryPosition — the implementation reads it from pull.meta (overview.ts:125-129, commented), which is the only surface exposing it; side effect is that every overview call performs a full pull render. (2) Tech design Flow 4 names listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from the report entries' queue joins instead — consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts, which is arguably stronger for AC-4.5, but the tech design was not updated to record either substitution.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Approved public-contract deviations are implemented exactly as ruled: loadCost.bandTokens measured from pull-served band messages rather than stored sums (ruling-011 Story 3; AC-2.3's equality is the governing contract and the shared/inspect.ts comment documents why stored sums structurally cannot match), and sourceState/meta nullable for never-compacted threads.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Error model and CLI conventions inherited cleanly: one additive caller_error code (invalid_bounds, Story 1 approved ruling, Epic 03 precedent), no other additions; CLI commands are thin argv-to-SDK wrappers with semantic validation kept in the SDK so parity including refusals is structural (cli/inspect.ts, cli/messages-read.ts).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"All 23 ACs and 17 TCs are implemented and traceable: test describe blocks name their TC/AC pairs explicitly across inspect-overview.test.ts (TC-1.1–1.3), inspect-view.test.ts (TC-2.1–2.3 + describe purity legs), messages-read.test.ts (TC-3.1–3.3 + three architecture-risk suites), inspect-health.test.ts (TC-4.1–4.3 + provider-free leg), lifecycle.test.ts (TC-5.1–5.3 with all four AC-5.2 checkpoint assertions including the receipt-vs-health cross-check), and cli-process-inspect.test.ts (TC-3.4, TC-5.4, process suite).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3/AC-5.4 materialized-file equality ships as threadId-normalized equality per approved Story 4 ruling-011: thread id is the design's one random value, the test substitutes only it and requires every other byte identical, with Date frozen so pull-output hash equality stays literal with zero normalization. The relaxation is principled, documented in the test header, and recorded in the story spec.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Zero-provider NFR is verified structurally for the whole epic: inspect/list/show/describe run green under a throwing provider, and the lifecycle's only provider is the registry's deterministic one (zero network, zero real-provider calls — AC-5.1).\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic gate run by this reviewer: pnpm verify-all PASS, exit 0, 366/366 tests across 44 files with the process suite executed (LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 is baked into verify-all), build/typecheck/lint/boundaries all green.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Closeout items still owed per the epic's own assumptions: the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic must be recorded at closeout, and the search-deferral PRD/tech-arch backfill exists but is uncommitted (see unresolvedItems).\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No fake adapters, shims, or placeholder execution paths remain on any production path. Grep for stub/placeholder/not-implemented across src/ finds only SQL parameter placeholders, comments, and the not_implemented code's vocabulary entry in shared/errors.ts — no operation returns it anymore; the Story 2 inspect.view stub was replaced by the real implementation in Story 3.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Provider posture is honest by construction: the registry (src/providers/registry.ts) contains exactly one provider — deterministic — which is the spec'd v1 state (real inference is explicitly next-PRD scope, carried in the epic's Out of Scope). There is no default provider: the CLI resolves only an explicitly named provider (--provider/LHC_PROVIDER) and fails with provider_not_configured rather than silently substituting the deterministic one.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"The lifecycle exercise runs the real production SDK (createSdk) in background mode through the production registry's deterministic provider and the real drainSettled awaitable — no test-only seams in the sequence itself; the one test-only control is freezing Date in the test file, which is outside the production path.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Stale comment, cosmetic only: src/cli/index.ts:473-475 still describes 'inspect view' as a not-implemented stub that 'Story 3 makes real' — Story 3 landed, the route is real, and the command is in the help text. The comment is now false; the code is correct.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic-level docs still carry literal 'byte-identical' phrasing superseded by approved ruling-011 (threadId-normalized file equality)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic.md AC-5.3/TC-5.2 (lines 149, 156-157), test-plan.md TC-5.2 (line 38), and coverage.md line 48 state byte-identical materialized-file equality; Story 4 ruling-011 (approved, recorded in team-impl-log.md and stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md) relaxed file equality to substitute the one random thread id, with pull-output hash equality remaining literal. The impl log itself flags this for epic-review awareness. The shipped test (lifecycle.test.ts:17-22, 97-104) implements the ruled contract correctly; only the epic-level docs lag.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/coverage.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-5.2\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Tech design not backfilled for two surface-respecting mechanism substitutions (overview boundary via pull.meta; health queue via report join)\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"tech-design.md DD-5 says overview takes boundary/zone 'via status', but ViewStatus (src/shared/view.ts:128-135) exposes no boundaryPosition — overview.ts:125-129 reads it from pull.meta, the only surface that exposes it, at the cost of a full pull render per overview call. Tech-design Flow 4 and the System View name listQueuedWork as a health input, but health.ts derives queue counts from FormReportEntry queue joins (consistent-by-construction with the same report's state counts). Both substitutions stay on surfaces and satisfy their ACs; neither is recorded as a design deviation.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/overview.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-1.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false},{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"E04-ER1-003\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"observation\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Stale stub-era comment on the 'inspect view' CLI route\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"src/cli/index.ts:473-475 says the route is 'routed ahead of its story so the CLI mirrors the SDK surface: the stub returns the structured not-implemented result; Story 3 makes it real (and adds it to the help text)' — Story 3 landed; runInspectView is the real implementation and the command appears in the help text (line 72). Comment is false, code is correct.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/cli/index.ts\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Uncommitted working-tree changes carry the sanctioned PRD AC-4.3 search-deferral backfill (packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/00-prd.md, 01-tech-arch.md) plus impl-log state bookkeeping — these are epic-mandated doc changes (epic.md Out of Scope: 'backfilled with this epic') and should be committed as part of epic closeout.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Epic closeout must record the M3/M4 quality-half transfer to the inference epic explicitly (epic.md Assumptions: 'Closeout records this explicitly') — not yet written; this review is upstream of that closeout step.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"},{\\\\\\\"resultId\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"7037aa32-e09d-4f0a-b954-6917da95a54b\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"block\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"provider\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"codex\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"model\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"gpt-5.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"reviewerLabel\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-reviewer-2\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"crossStoryFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Stories 1-4 are wired through the SDK and CLI and the configured gates pass: `pnpm verify` passed with 328 tests and `pnpm verify-all` passed with 366 tests / 44 files, including the process suite.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Flow 4 has unresolved cross-story semantic drift: `inspect.health.queue` reports one queued/claimed count per pending form report entry, while the epic and tech design describe queued/claimed work counts from owner queue detail. A turn-derivation work item that owns two forms is counted twice by health.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"architectureFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"`domains/inspect/**` imports owner surfaces only; `check-boundaries` passed and the inspect source check found no raw SQL/table access in inspect.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"`inspect.view` and lifecycle determinism intentionally follow approved rulings, but the epic-level artifacts still contain older wording for materialized-file byte identity and the tech design still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the stored band-count sum.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"epicCoverageAssessment\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Most epic ACs have direct default/process suite coverage across `messages-read`, `inspect-overview`, `inspect-health`, `inspect-view`, `lifecycle`, and `cli-process-inspect`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-4.5 is not conclusively covered because the tests assert consistency with pending form-entry counts, not queue-detail work-item counts.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"productionPathFindings\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"No material fake adapter, shim, placeholder, or non-real production execution path was found in the audited SDK/CLI inspect, message-read, thread-view, and lifecycle paths.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"Material production-path issue: `inspect.health` derives queue counts from `FormReportEntry.queue` per form entry and does not count live queue work rows; on a mutation-in-flight production fixture it returned `{queued:5, claimed:0}` while owner `listQueuedWork` surfaces showed four live work items.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"blockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-001\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"major\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Health queue counts do not match queue-detail work counts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Epic AC-4.5 requires queued and claimed work counts from owner queue detail; tech-design Flow 4 says `health` composes `messages.report` + `turns.report` + `listQueuedWork` both owners. In `src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts:40-105`, `composeHealth` only reads `messages.report` and `turns.report`, then increments `queue` once for every report entry with `entry.queue` at lines 89-95. In an ad hoc mutation-in-flight fixture, `inspect.health` returned `healthQueue:{queued:5,claimed:0}` while `messages.listQueuedWork` + `turns.listQueuedWork` returned four work item ids: `w-m5-prompt_smoothing-v2`, `w-t2-turn_derivation-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_brief-v2`, `w-c1-chunk_summary_detailed-v2`.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/src/domains/inspect/internal/health.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/inspect-health.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/test/lifecycle.test.ts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-4.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"TC-4.1\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"tech-design Flow 4: Health\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"human-ruling\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":true}],\\\\\\\"nonBlockingFindings\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"EV-04-002\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"minor\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"title\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Accepted deviation wording is not propagated through all epic-level artifacts\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Story 4 and ruling-011 accept materialized-file equality after substituting only the random threadId, and tests implement that in `test/lifecycle.test.ts:97-103` and `:282-302`. The epic and test plan still say materialized files are byte-identical without that qualifier at `epic.md:149-157` and `test-plan.md:38-39`. Story 3/ruling-011 accepts measured pull-served `loadCost.bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState`, while `tech-design.md:94` still says `loadCost.bandTokens` is the sum of stored band counts and `stories/03-view-contents-report.md:119-121` still says no deviations.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"affectedFiles\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/03-view-contents-report.md\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/stories/04-lifecycle-exercise.md\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"requirementIds\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"AC-2.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-2.5\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.3\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"AC-5.4\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"recommendedFixScope\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"quick-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"blocking\\\\\\\":false}],\\\\\\\"unresolvedItems\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\"Decide whether `HealthReport.queue` is intended to count live work items or pending/retrying form entries. The current implementation and tests use form-entry counts; the epic/tech-design wording points to queue-detail work counts.\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\"gateResult\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"pass\\\\\\\"}]},\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"artifacts\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"result-envelope\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/001-epic-review.json\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"startedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:43:43.996Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finishedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:54:28.853Z\\\\\\\"}\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":2,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":2}}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:38:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01BNNJTAK1uEH3PoMhRhJjxc\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t# Epic 04: Inspection\\\\n2\\\\t\\\\n3\\\\t**Status:** Validated — ready for story publishing and tech design\\\\n4\\\\t**PRD:** `../00-prd.md` Feature 4\\\\n5\\\\t**Tech Arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md`\\\\n6\\\\t**Depends on:** Epic 01 (record and read-back), Epic 02 (report/requeue surfaces, mutation cascade), Epic 03 (view storage, status, pull — in build; consumed as spec'd)\\\\n7\\\\t**Counts:** 23 ACs / 17 TCs across 5 flows\\\\n8\\\\t\\\\n9\\\\t## Onboarding Context\\\\n10\\\\t\\\\n11\\\\tRead first: `../../01-onboard/02-domain-design.md` §Inspect (the domain's charter: read-only, reads through other domains' surfaces, never writes, repairs, or derives), §Messages (read ownership), §Thread view (the view state this epic reports on). The Epic 02 spec pack defines the report surfaces this epic composes (`messages.report`, `turns.report`, queue detail). The Epic 03 spec pack defines the view storage and status shapes the view-contents report reads.\\\\n12\\\\t\\\\n13\\\\tThis is the last epic of the v1 PRD. It adds no tables, no migration, no derivations, and no provider use. It completes the read side of the product and closes with a full-surface lifecycle exercise — the first time every epic's surface runs in one sequence.\\\\n14\\\\t\\\\n15\\\\t## User Profile\\\\n16\\\\t\\\\n17\\\\t**Primary user:** the operator (Lee, mentees later) auditing threads from the CLI; secondarily, agents inside a harness using the same reads mid-task, and — for Flow 5 only — the future PI extension, whose call order the lifecycle exercise rehearses.\\\\n18\\\\t\\\\n19\\\\t**Context:** the operator arrives with a question — what does this thread hold, what did the agent actually see, did the rebuild land, why is this view degraded — and acts on the answer with Feature 2's mutation and requeue operations. Inspect tells them where to point those.\\\\n20\\\\t\\\\n21\\\\t**Mental model:** \\\\\\\"inspect describes; it never changes. Every report reads the same state the serving surfaces read, so a report never disagrees with what the agent was actually served. When a report names a subject, I can drill to it — view entry → chunk → turn → message → blocks.\\\\\\\"\\\\n22\\\\t\\\\n23\\\\t**Key constraint:** read-only, structurally — no inspect operation writes rows, transitions state, or moves the boundary; and no operation in this epic invokes a provider. Reports compose the owning domains' surfaces; inspect owns no rows and reads no other domain's tables directly.\\\\n24\\\\t\\\\n25\\\\t## Feature Overview\\\\n26\\\\t\\\\n27\\\\tInspection answers questions about a thread without changing it. Four reads: a thread overview (size, composition, derivation state at a glance), a view-contents report (what the active view holds, entry by entry, and what loading it costs), message listing and viewing (the drill-down target every other report points into), and a derivation health report (counts by state, failures with reasons, what repair would touch). Plus the lifecycle exercise: the whole SDK surface driven end-to-end in PI-extension call order.\\\\n28\\\\t\\\\n29\\\\tEverything here reads through the owning domains' surfaces. Inspect owns no rows. The one surface addition outside the inspect domain: `thread-view` gains a read-only `describe` operation exposing the stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, provenance), because inspect may not read `thread_view` tables directly and no existing operation exposes them.\\\\n30\\\\t\\\\n31\\\\t### Flow Summary\\\\n32\\\\t\\\\n33\\\\t| Flow | Name | Surface |\\\\n34\\\\t|------|------|---------|\\\\n35\\\\t| 1 | Thread overview | `inspect.overview` |\\\\n36\\\\t| 2 | View contents and load cost | `inspect.view` (+ `threadView.describe`) |\\\\n37\\\\t| 3 | Message listing and viewing | `messages.list` / `messages.show` |\\\\n38\\\\t| 4 | Derivation health and rebuild visibility | `inspect.health` |\\\\n39\\\\t| 5 | Full-surface lifecycle exercise | test-only; no new surface |\\\\n40\\\\t\\\\n41\\\\t## Scope\\\\n42\\\\t\\\\n43\\\\t### In Scope\\\\n44\\\\t\\\\n45\\\\t- `inspect` domain surface: `overview`, `view`, `health` — read-only composition over owning domains' reports\\\\n46\\\\t- `threadView.describe`: read-only exposure of the stored active view (arrangement entries, gaps, config, source-state provenance)\\\\n47\\\\t- Message read completion on the `messages` surface: listing options (bounds, include-deleted) and single-message view with blocks and derivation form states\\\\n48\\\\t- CLI: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list` (extended), `lhc messages show` — JSON, SDK-parity, process-suite legs\\\\n49\\\\t- The lifecycle exercise: create → intake → drain → status → compact → pull → inspect → mutate → rebuild → compact → pull → materialize, through the real SDK, deterministic provider, with replay-equality and instance-teardown legs\\\\n50\\\\t\\\\n51\\\\t### Out of Scope\\\\n52\\\\t\\\\n53\\\\t- **Message search — deferred post-v1.** No search ships in v1. The shape (substring vs FTS, ranking, result granularity) gets decided from real usage after LHC and the PI extension are integrated. The PRD and tech arch carry this deferral (Feature 4 scope, Future Directions, tech-arch deferred list) — backfilled with this epic, so tech design inherits no contradiction.\\\\n54\\\\t- Mutations and repair execution (Feature 2 owns; inspect reports on them and previews repair, never executes)\\\\n55\\\\t- Any new derivation, any provider call, any real inference (next PRD cycle owns the inference feature)\\\\n56\\\\t- The PI extension itself (next PRD)\\\\n57\\\\t- Watch/follow modes, streaming output, UI rendering — CLI is JSON one-shots\\\\n58\\\\t- Cross-thread reports (single thread scope, same as every epic)\\\\n59\\\\t\\\\n60\\\\t### Assumptions\\\\n61\\\\t\\\\n62\\\\t- Epic 03 is in build. This epic consumes its surfaces as spec'd (`status`, `pull`, view storage shapes). **Handoff gate:** before this epic's tech design freezes, the tech design must check Epic 02's and Epic 03's final deviation tables and update every consumed contract this epic references; the tech design records that check's outcome in its Spec Validation table.\\\\n63\\\\t- Epic 03's Story 0 fixture (deterministic provider, ~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle, manufactured failure states) is reusable here and extends with mutation-in-flight states; no new fixture family.\\\\n64\\\\t- Schema is terminal at v6 for this PRD: this epic ships **no migration**. If tech design finds a needed index, that is a v7 migration decision to surface, not assume.\\\\n65\\\\t- The deleted-message contract is Epic 02's, inherited: deleted messages drop from reads, source events retain the originals. This epic adds the audit option to see them, not a new policy.\\\\n66\\\\t- M3/M4 milestone gates close mechanically only: view *quality* cannot be reviewed while bands render deterministic-provider output. The quality halves of those gates transfer to the inference feature's epic. Closeout records this explicitly.\\\\n67\\\\t\\\\n68\\\\t## Flow 1: Thread Overview\\\\n69\\\\t\\\\n70\\\\tOne call answers \\\\\\\"what is this thread\\\\\\\": identity, record size, composition, derivation state, view state, visibility state. The numbers an operator scans before deciding to compact, repair, or drill in.\\\\n71\\\\t\\\\n72\\\\t#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n73\\\\t\\\\n74\\\\t- **AC-1.1**: `inspect.overview` returns, in one read-only call: thread identity and metadata; event count and order span; message counts (total visible, by kind, deleted counted separately) with visible token sum; turn counts (open, closed); chunk count and closed-but-unchunked turn count; derivation counts by state (pending, retrying, failed, blocked, ready); active-view summary (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) or null when never compacted; visibility boundary position and current zone token sum.\\\\n75\\\\t- **AC-1.2**: Counts honor the deleted contract: deleted messages appear only in the deleted count — excluded from visible counts, kind breakdowns, and token sums; event counts are unaffected (the record retains everything).\\\\n76\\\\t- **AC-1.3**: Every thread shape reports cleanly: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted, compacted, mid-rebuild. Absent pieces report as zeros or null — never omitted fields, never shape errors.\\\\n77\\\\t- **AC-1.4**: The overview is a pure read: no work items created, no state changed, repeated calls with no intervening writes return identical results.\\\\n78\\\\t\\\\n79\\\\t#### Test Conditions\\\\n80\\\\t\\\\n81\\\\t- **TC-1.1** (AC-1.1, AC-1.3): Overview shape variants: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls. The compacted tool-heavy fixture asserts exact expected counts (messages by kind, turns, chunks, derivation states, view summary, boundary).\\\\n82\\\\t- **TC-1.2** (AC-1.2): Delete one message; overview → visible count and token sum drop, deleted count = 1, kind breakdown excludes it, event count unchanged.\\\\n83\\\\t- **TC-1.3** (AC-1.4): Overview twice with no writes between → deep-equal results; no `work_item` rows created; zero provider calls.\\\\n84\\\\t\\\\n85\\\\t## Flow 2: View Contents and Load Cost\\\\n86\\\\t\\\\n87\\\\tWhat the agent actually sees, and what it costs. The report reads the stored active view (via `threadView.describe`) and the live tail, entry by entry, with the cost a pull would incur right now.\\\\n88\\\\t\\\\n89\\\\t#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n90\\\\t\\\\n91\\\\t- **AC-2.1**: The report names the active view — viewId, createdAt, profile name and resolved config, compactPoint, coveredFrom — and lists every band entry in served order (brief → detailed → smooth): subject kind and id, form used, degraded flag; plus every gap with its reason; plus per-band stored token counts. All of it from the stored snapshot, not recomputed.\\\\n92\\\\t- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\\\\n93\\\\t- **AC-2.3**: `loadCost` totals what `pull` serves now — bands plus tail — and a test asserts equality against an actual pull's measured content. The report never disagrees with the surface it describes.\\\\n94\\\\t- **AC-2.4**: A never-compacted thread reports view: null with a tail-only loadCost under the same equality contract (the whole record served as tail).\\\\n95\\\\t- **AC-2.5**: The report carries the view's recorded source-state provenance (what the compact saw: max event order, form counts) and is a pure read under AC-1.4's contract.\\\\n96\\\\t\\\\n97\\\\t#### Test Conditions\\\\n98\\\\t\\\\n99\\\\t- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1, AC-2.5): On a compacted fixture with one degraded entry and one gap → report matches the stored arrangement exactly: subjects, forms used, degraded flags, gap reasons, band token counts, config, provenance.\\\\n100\\\\t- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3): On a boundary-advanced fixture → tail cost counts short forms short; `loadCost.total` equals the token measure of an actual `pull`'s messages using the same estimator.\\\\n101\\\\t- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): Never-compacted thread → view null, tail spans the record, cost-parity assertion holds.\\\\n102\\\\t\\\\n103\\\\t## Flow 3: Message Listing and Viewing\\\\n104\\\\t\\\\n105\\\\tThe drill-down floor. Every report names subjects; this flow is where an operator or agent reads the actual record. Epic 01 shipped `listMessages` bare; this flow completes it and adds the single-message view.\\\\n106\\\\t\\\\n107\\\\t#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n108\\\\t\\\\n109\\\\t- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\\\n110\\\\t- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\\\n111\\\\t- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\\\n112\\\\t- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\\\n113\\\\t\\\\n114\\\\t#### Test Conditions\\\\n115\\\\t\\\\n116\\\\t- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\\\n117\\\\t- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\\\n118\\\\t- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\\\n119\\\\t- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\\\n120\\\\t\\\\n121\\\\t## Flow 4: Derivation Health and Rebuild Visibility\\\\n122\\\\t\\\\n123\\\\tThe state of every derived form, aggregated to act on. This is also where a mutation's rebuild is watched: cleared forms show pending with queued work, then land ready.\\\\n124\\\\t\\\\n125\\\\t#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n126\\\\t\\\\n127\\\\t- **AC-4.1**: `inspect.health` aggregates across owners — counts by owner, form kind, and state (ready, pending, retrying, failed, blocked) — assembled entirely from the owners' report surfaces, never from direct `derived_form` or `work_item` reads.\\\\n128\\\\t- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\\\\n129\\\\t- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\\\\n130\\\\t- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\\\\n131\\\\t- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: `health.queue` reports queued and claimed counts **per form-report entry**, tallied from each entry's live queue-item join in the owners' reports — every pending/retrying form rides one live queue item, so `queued + claimed` equals `pending + retrying` in the same report by construction. These are per-entry counts, not raw `listQueuedWork` work-item counts: one `turn_derivation` work item can back multiple form entries, so a raw work-item count would break that identity.\\\\n132\\\\t\\\\n133\\\\t#### Test Conditions\\\\n134\\\\t\\\\n135\\\\t- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\\\\n136\\\\t- **TC-4.2** (AC-4.2, AC-4.3): Failed and blocked forms present → failure detail exact (subject, form, reason, attempts); repair preview lists exactly the failed-not-blocked set.\\\\n137\\\\t- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\\\\n138\\\\t\\\\n139\\\\t## Flow 5: Full-Surface Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n140\\\\t\\\\n141\\\\tNot a capstone — nothing here proves integration readiness, because no real inference exists yet (that gate belongs to the inference epic). This is the cross-epic seam proof: the first sequence that drives every surface the PI extension will call, in its call order, against one SDK instance. What it catches: contract drift between the three built epics' surfaces, lifecycle ordering bugs, state leaks between operations.\\\\n142\\\\t\\\\n143\\\\tThe sequence (PI-extension call order): create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\\\\n144\\\\t\\\\n145\\\\t#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n146\\\\t\\\\n147\\\\t- **AC-5.1**: The full sequence completes through one real SDK configuration with the deterministic provider: every operation returns ok, zero network, zero real-provider calls.\\\\n148\\\\t- **AC-5.2**: Checkpoint coherence: post-compact pull serves bands + tail; post-mutation health shows the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready; the second compact's view reflects post-edit content; the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it.\\\\n149\\\\t- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces literally byte-identical pull outputs (they carry no thread id, so equality is asserted with no normalization), and a materialized file byte-identical after normalizing only the intentionally random thread id — the two runs' thread ids are asserted to differ and every other byte must be exact (Story 4 ruling-011).\\\\n150\\\\t- **AC-5.4**: No in-memory dependency: tearing down the SDK instance between phases and continuing on a fresh `createSdk` yields the same end state as the uninterrupted run.\\\\n151\\\\t- **AC-5.5**: Operator parity: inspect and view reads driven through the spawned CLI at checkpoints return the same JSON as the in-process SDK calls at those checkpoints.\\\\n152\\\\t\\\\n153\\\\t#### Test Conditions\\\\n154\\\\t\\\\n155\\\\t- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Scripted lifecycle with checkpoint assertions at each named step; receipt-vs-health cross-check exact.\\\\n156\\\\t- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → literal hash equality on every pull output; materialized-file hash equality after substituting only the random thread id, asserting the two thread ids differ and every other byte is exact.\\\\n157\\\\t- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.4): Teardown and recreate the SDK between intake/compact/mutation phases → final pull and health identical to TC-5.1's, and the materialized file hash-equal after substituting only the random thread id (every other byte exact).\\\\n158\\\\t- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.5): Process-suite leg: spawned CLI inspect/view/messages reads at three checkpoints equal the in-process results.\\\\n159\\\\t\\\\n160\\\\t## Data Contracts\\\\n161\\\\t\\\\n162\\\\tContract-level shapes; field mechanics are tech design's. All operations `Promise<OpResult<...>>` taking `ThreadRef`; all read-only.\\\\n163\\\\t\\\\n164\\\\t**`InspectOverview`**: thread (id, createdAt, metadata); events (count, span); messages (visible count, byKind, deletedCount, visibleTokens); turns (open, closed); chunks (count, unchunkedTurns); derivation (counts by state); view (summary | null); visibility (boundaryPosition, zoneTokens).\\\\n165\\\\t\\\\n166\\\\t**`ViewContentsReport`**: meta (viewId, createdAt, profile, config, compactPoint, coveredFrom) | null; bands — ordered entries (subjectKind, subjectId, formUsed, degraded) and stored tokens per band; gaps (band, subjectId, reason); tail (messageCount, tokens as served); loadCost (bandTokens, tailTokens, total — equals what pull serves); sourceState (provenance as stored).\\\\n167\\\\t\\\\n168\\\\t**`threadView.describe`**: the stored active view row exposed read-only — arrangement, gaps, config, source state, identity/timestamps. Absent view → ok with null (not an error). This is the one surface addition outside inspect; it exists so inspect never touches `thread_view` tables.\\\\n169\\\\t\\\\n170\\\\t**`HealthReport`**: owners[] (owner, kind, counts by state); failures[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form, reason, attempts, lastError?); repairPreview[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form); queue (queued, claimed).\\\\n171\\\\t\\\\n172\\\\t**`MessageDetail`** (show): the full `MessageRecord` (all blocks, full content, token estimate, turnId, deleted flag) plus forms: the owner's report entries for this message.\\\\n173\\\\t\\\\n174\\\\t**List options**: bounded listing (range/limit) and includeDeleted; exact option names are tech design's, the *existence* of bounds and the deleted default are contract.\\\\n175\\\\t\\\\n176\\\\t**CLI**: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list [--include-deleted] [bounds]`, `lhc messages show --message-id <id>` — JSON to stdout, SDK-parity, same error classes as every epic (`caller_error`, `state_corruption`, `system_error`).\\\\n177\\\\t\\\\n178\\\\t## Non-Functional Requirements\\\\n179\\\\t\\\\n180\\\\t- **Read-only, structurally**: no inspect operation writes — no work rows, no state transitions, no boundary movement. Asserted, not assumed.\\\\n181\\\\t- **No inference in this epic**: no Epic 04 operation invokes a provider; tests may use Epic 02 deterministic-provider setup (draining queued work through the fake) to prepare the derived states under test.\\\\n182\\\\t- **Local and fast**: reports compose domain-surface reads over one thread file; no network, no scans proportional to anything but the thread.\\\\n183\\\\t- **Consistency with served reality**: where a report describes another surface's output (loadCost vs pull), equality is contractual and tested, not aspirational.\\\\n184\\\\t\\\\n185\\\\t## Tech Design Questions\\\\n186\\\\t\\\\n187\\\\t1. `messages.show` shape: new operation vs `listMessages` option — and whether the forms join reuses `messages.report(messageId)` internally or a shared internal read.\\\\n188\\\\t2. `threadView.describe` mapping: stored row → report shape, and whether `describe` and `inspect.view` share assembly code with `status` (they read overlapping state).\\\\n189\\\\t3. `loadCost` mechanism: measure by internally invoking `pull` vs summing the same sources pull reads — equality is the contract either way; pick for cost and locality.\\\\n190\\\\t4. Health assembly: per-owner report calls composed in inspect vs a shared internal join — must stay on surfaces either way.\\\\n191\\\\t5. Lifecycle exercise placement: which legs run in the default suite (TC-5.1 likely) vs the process suite (TC-5.2/5.3/5.4), and where the scripted sequence lives so both legs share it.\\\\n192\\\\t6. Listing bounds: offset/limit vs event-order range — pick from CLI ergonomics; both bounded.\\\\n193\\\\t\\\\n194\\\\t## Story Breakdown\\\\n195\\\\t\\\\n196\\\\tNo Story 0, decided not defaulted: Story-0s exist to land shared substrate that multiple stories would otherwise each half-build — migrations, new tables, config plumbing, fixture families (Epics 01–03 each had at least one of these). This epic has none. The foundation work that does exist is single-consumer and lands with its consumer: the `inspect` surface skeleton and report shapes belong to Story 2 (shapes live in `shared/` per house pattern, so Story 3 consumes without redefining), `threadView.describe` belongs to Story 3 (its only caller is `inspect.view`), and the fixture extension for mutation-in-flight states belongs to Story 2 (its first consumer). A foundation story here would own no checkable behavior of its own. Four stories.\\\\n197\\\\t\\\\n198\\\\t### Story 1: Message Read Surface\\\\n199\\\\t\\\\n200\\\\tCompletes Flow 3: listing options, `show` with forms join, deleted-audit option, CLI extension + parity. Depends only on built code (Epics 01–02). ACs: 3.1–3.4. TCs: 3.1–3.4. ~7 tests.\\\\n201\\\\t\\\\n202\\\\t### Story 2: Inspect Domain — Overview and Health\\\\n203\\\\t\\\\n204\\\\tThe `inspect` domain is born: surface skeleton, `overview` and `health` composed from owners' reports, CLI commands, fixture extension for mutation-in-flight states. Flows 1 and 4. ACs: 1.1–1.4, 4.1–4.5. TCs: 1.1–1.3, 4.1–4.3. ~9 tests.\\\\n205\\\\t\\\\n206\\\\t### Story 3: View-Contents Report\\\\n207\\\\t\\\\n208\\\\t`threadView.describe` (read-only surface addition) + `inspect.view` with the loadCost-equals-pull contract. Flow 2. Depends on Epic 03 Stories 0–2 landed (view storage exists). ACs: 2.1–2.5. TCs: 2.1–2.3. ~6 tests.\\\\n209\\\\t\\\\n210\\\\t### Story 4: Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n211\\\\t\\\\n212\\\\tThe scripted full-surface sequence with checkpoint, replay, teardown, and CLI-parity legs. Flow 5. Depends on Stories 1–3 here plus Epic 03 complete. ACs: 5.1–5.5. TCs: 5.1–5.4. ~6 tests.\\\\n213\\\\t\\\\n214\\\\t**Sequencing**: Story 1 can start immediately (no Epic 03 dependency). Story 2 next (fixture states; health consumes built reports). Story 3 waits on Epic 03's view storage stories. Story 4 last. If Epic 03's build slips, Stories 1–2 proceed; 3–4 wait.\\\\n215\\\\t\\\\n216\\\\t## Traceability\\\\n217\\\\t\\\\n218\\\\t| PRD | This epic |\\\\n219\\\\t|-----|-----------|\\\\n220\\\\t| AC-4.1 (view contents and cost) | Flow 2 |\\\\n221\\\\t| AC-4.2 (messages listable/viewable) | Flow 3 |\\\\n222\\\\t| PRD AC-4.3 (search) | **Deferred post-v1** — Out of Scope; PRD and tech arch already backfilled |\\\\n223\\\\t| AC-4.4 (rebuild visibility) | Flow 4 (AC-4.4) |\\\\n224\\\\t| AC-4.5 (derivation health) | Flow 4 (AC-4.1–4.3, 4.5) |\\\\n225\\\\t| Feature 4 scope: \\\\\\\"thread size and composition, turn and chunk counts\\\\\\\" | Flow 1 |\\\\n226\\\\t| M4 \\\\\\\"SDK exercised end-to-end at its integration points\\\\\\\" | Flow 5 (mechanical half; quality half transfers to the inference epic) |\\\\n227\\\\t\\\\n228\\\\t### AC → TC Table\\\\n229\\\\t\\\\n230\\\\t| AC | TCs |\\\\n231\\\\t|----|-----|\\\\n232\\\\t| AC-1.1 | TC-1.1 |\\\\n233\\\\t| AC-1.2 | TC-1.2 |\\\\n234\\\\t| AC-1.3 | TC-1.1 |\\\\n235\\\\t| AC-1.4 | TC-1.3 |\\\\n236\\\\t| AC-2.1 | TC-2.1 |\\\\n237\\\\t| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2 |\\\\n238\\\\t| AC-2.3 | TC-2.2 |\\\\n239\\\\t| AC-2.4 | TC-2.3 |\\\\n240\\\\t| AC-2.5 | TC-2.1 |\\\\n241\\\\t| AC-3.1 | TC-3.1 |\\\\n242\\\\t| AC-3.2 | TC-3.2 |\\\\n243\\\\t| AC-3.3 | TC-3.3 |\\\\n244\\\\t| AC-3.4 | TC-3.4 |\\\\n245\\\\t| AC-4.1 | TC-4.1 |\\\\n246\\\\t| AC-4.2 | TC-4.2 |\\\\n247\\\\t| AC-4.3 | TC-4.2 |\\\\n248\\\\t| AC-4.4 | TC-4.3 |\\\\n249\\\\t| AC-4.5 | TC-4.1 |\\\\n250\\\\t| AC-5.1 | TC-5.1 |\\\\n251\\\\t| AC-5.2 | TC-5.1 |\\\\n252\\\\t| AC-5.3 | TC-5.2 |\\\\n253\\\\t| AC-5.4 | TC-5.3 |\\\\n254\\\\t| AC-5.5 | TC-5.4 |\\\\n255\\\\t\\\\n256\\\\t## Completeness Self-Check\\\\n257\\\\t\\\\n258\\\\t- [ ] Every PRD Feature 4 AC mapped or explicitly deferred (PRD AC-4.3 search deferred, named, with PRD/tech-arch deferral recorded)\\\\n259\\\\t- [ ] Every flow has ACs and TCs; every AC covered by at least one TC (23/23 per table)\\\\n260\\\\t- [ ] No TC references an undefined AC\\\\n261\\\\t- [ ] Read-only contract stated per flow and as NFR\\\\n262\\\\t- [ ] No new storage, no migration — stated as assumption\\\\n263\\\\t- [ ] Epic 03 in-build dependency named with deviation-table check before tech design freeze\\\\n264\\\\t- [ ] Lifecycle exercise scoped as seam proof, not integration gate; M3/M4 quality-half transfer recorded\\\\n265\\\\t- [ ] No Epic 04 operation invokes inference; provider use only in Epic 02 test setup wording carried\\\\n266\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"edc584b8-9c27-46b5-a766-9ebfb7408b74\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:04:02.827Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/epic.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Epic 04: Inspection\\\\n\\\\n**Status:** Validated — ready for story publishing and tech design\\\\n**PRD:** `../00-prd.md` Feature 4\\\\n**Tech Arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md`\\\\n**Depends on:** Epic 01 (record and read-back), Epic 02 (report/requeue surfaces, mutation cascade), Epic 03 (view storage, status, pull — in build; consumed as spec'd)\\\\n**Counts:** 23 ACs / 17 TCs across 5 flows\\\\n\\\\n## Onboarding Context\\\\n\\\\nRead first: `../../01-onboard/02-domain-design.md` §Inspect (the domain's charter: read-only, reads through other domains' surfaces, never writes, repairs, or derives), §Messages (read ownership), §Thread view (the view state this epic reports on). The Epic 02 spec pack defines the report surfaces this epic composes (`messages.report`, `turns.report`, queue detail). The Epic 03 spec pack defines the view storage and status shapes the view-contents report reads.\\\\n\\\\nThis is the last epic of the v1 PRD. It adds no tables, no migration, no derivations, and no provider use. It completes the read side of the product and closes with a full-surface lifecycle exercise — the first time every epic's surface runs in one sequence.\\\\n\\\\n## User Profile\\\\n\\\\n**Primary user:** the operator (Lee, mentees later) auditing threads from the CLI; secondarily, agents inside a harness using the same reads mid-task, and — for Flow 5 only — the future PI extension, whose call order the lifecycle exercise rehearses.\\\\n\\\\n**Context:** the operator arrives with a question — what does this thread hold, what did the agent actually see, did the rebuild land, why is this view degraded — and acts on the answer with Feature 2's mutation and requeue operations. Inspect tells them where to point those.\\\\n\\\\n**Mental model:** \\\\\\\"inspect describes; it never changes. Every report reads the same state the serving surfaces read, so a report never disagrees with what the agent was actually served. When a report names a subject, I can drill to it — view entry → chunk → turn → message → blocks.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Key constraint:** read-only, structurally — no inspect operation writes rows, transitions state, or moves the boundary; and no operation in this epic invokes a provider. Reports compose the owning domains' surfaces; inspect owns no rows and reads no other domain's tables directly.\\\\n\\\\n## Feature Overview\\\\n\\\\nInspection answers questions about a thread without changing it. Four reads: a thread overview (size, composition, derivation state at a glance), a view-contents report (what the active view holds, entry by entry, and what loading it costs), message listing and viewing (the drill-down target every other report points into), and a derivation health report (counts by state, failures with reasons, what repair would touch). Plus the lifecycle exercise: the whole SDK surface driven end-to-end in PI-extension call order.\\\\n\\\\nEverything here reads through the owning domains' surfaces. Inspect owns no rows. The one surface addition outside the inspect domain: `thread-view` gains a read-only `describe` operation exposing the stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, provenance), because inspect may not read `thread_view` tables directly and no existing operation exposes them.\\\\n\\\\n### Flow Summary\\\\n\\\\n| Flow | Name | Surface |\\\\n|------|------|---------|\\\\n| 1 | Thread overview | `inspect.overview` |\\\\n| 2 | View contents and load cost | `inspect.view` (+ `threadView.describe`) |\\\\n| 3 | Message listing and viewing | `messages.list` / `messages.show` |\\\\n| 4 | Derivation health and rebuild visibility | `inspect.health` |\\\\n| 5 | Full-surface lifecycle exercise | test-only; no new surface |\\\\n\\\\n## Scope\\\\n\\\\n### In Scope\\\\n\\\\n- `inspect` domain surface: `overview`, `view`, `health` — read-only composition over owning domains' reports\\\\n- `threadView.describe`: read-only exposure of the stored active view (arrangement entries, gaps, config, source-state provenance)\\\\n- Message read completion on the `messages` surface: listing options (bounds, include-deleted) and single-message view with blocks and derivation form states\\\\n- CLI: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list` (extended), `lhc messages show` — JSON, SDK-parity, process-suite legs\\\\n- The lifecycle exercise: create → intake → drain → status → compact → pull → inspect → mutate → rebuild → compact → pull → materialize, through the real SDK, deterministic provider, with replay-equality and instance-teardown legs\\\\n\\\\n### Out of Scope\\\\n\\\\n- **Message search — deferred post-v1.** No search ships in v1. The shape (substring vs FTS, ranking, result granularity) gets decided from real usage after LHC and the PI extension are integrated. The PRD and tech arch carry this deferral (Feature 4 scope, Future Directions, tech-arch deferred list) — backfilled with this epic, so tech design inherits no contradiction.\\\\n- Mutations and repair execution (Feature 2 owns; inspect reports on them and previews repair, never executes)\\\\n- Any new derivation, any provider call, any real inference (next PRD cycle owns the inference feature)\\\\n- The PI extension itself (next PRD)\\\\n- Watch/follow modes, streaming output, UI rendering — CLI is JSON one-shots\\\\n- Cross-thread reports (single thread scope, same as every epic)\\\\n\\\\n### Assumptions\\\\n\\\\n- Epic 03 is in build. This epic consumes its surfaces as spec'd (`status`, `pull`, view storage shapes). **Handoff gate:** before this epic's tech design freezes, the tech design must check Epic 02's and Epic 03's final deviation tables and update every consumed contract this epic references; the tech design records that check's outcome in its Spec Validation table.\\\\n- Epic 03's Story 0 fixture (deterministic provider, ~12 turns, 4 chunks, tool-heavy middle, manufactured failure states) is reusable here and extends with mutation-in-flight states; no new fixture family.\\\\n- Schema is terminal at v6 for this PRD: this epic ships **no migration**. If tech design finds a needed index, that is a v7 migration decision to surface, not assume.\\\\n- The deleted-message contract is Epic 02's, inherited: deleted messages drop from reads, source events retain the originals. This epic adds the audit option to see them, not a new policy.\\\\n- M3/M4 milestone gates close mechanically only: view *quality* cannot be reviewed while bands render deterministic-provider output. The quality halves of those gates transfer to the inference feature's epic. Closeout records this explicitly.\\\\n\\\\n## Flow 1: Thread Overview\\\\n\\\\nOne call answers \\\\\\\"what is this thread\\\\\\\": identity, record size, composition, derivation state, view state, visibility state. The numbers an operator scans before deciding to compact, repair, or drill in.\\\\n\\\\n#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-1.1**: `inspect.overview` returns, in one read-only call: thread identity and metadata; event count and order span; message counts (total visible, by kind, deleted counted separately) with visible token sum; turn counts (open, closed); chunk count and closed-but-unchunked turn count; derivation counts by state (pending, retrying, failed, blocked, ready); active-view summary (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) or null when never compacted; visibility boundary position and current zone token sum.\\\\n- **AC-1.2**: Counts honor the deleted contract: deleted messages appear only in the deleted count — excluded from visible counts, kind breakdowns, and token sums; event counts are unaffected (the record retains everything).\\\\n- **AC-1.3**: Every thread shape reports cleanly: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted, compacted, mid-rebuild. Absent pieces report as zeros or null — never omitted fields, never shape errors.\\\\n- **AC-1.4**: The overview is a pure read: no work items created, no state changed, repeated calls with no intervening writes return identical results.\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Conditions\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-1.1** (AC-1.1, AC-1.3): Overview shape variants: fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls. The compacted tool-heavy fixture asserts exact expected counts (messages by kind, turns, chunks, derivation states, view summary, boundary).\\\\n- **TC-1.2** (AC-1.2): Delete one message; overview → visible count and token sum drop, deleted count = 1, kind breakdown excludes it, event count unchanged.\\\\n- **TC-1.3** (AC-1.4): Overview twice with no writes between → deep-equal results; no `work_item` rows created; zero provider calls.\\\\n\\\\n## Flow 2: View Contents and Load Cost\\\\n\\\\nWhat the agent actually sees, and what it costs. The report reads the stored active view (via `threadView.describe`) and the live tail, entry by entry, with the cost a pull would incur right now.\\\\n\\\\n#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-2.1**: The report names the active view — viewId, createdAt, profile name and resolved config, compactPoint, coveredFrom — and lists every band entry in served order (brief → detailed → smooth): subject kind and id, form used, degraded flag; plus every gap with its reason; plus per-band stored token counts. All of it from the stored snapshot, not recomputed.\\\\n- **AC-2.2**: The tail section reports message count and token cost *as currently served*: tool results at-or-behind the visibility boundary are costed at their short form, everything else full.\\\\n- **AC-2.3**: `loadCost` totals what `pull` serves now — bands plus tail — and a test asserts equality against an actual pull's measured content. The report never disagrees with the surface it describes.\\\\n- **AC-2.4**: A never-compacted thread reports view: null with a tail-only loadCost under the same equality contract (the whole record served as tail).\\\\n- **AC-2.5**: The report carries the view's recorded source-state provenance (what the compact saw: max event order, form counts) and is a pure read under AC-1.4's contract.\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Conditions\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-2.1** (AC-2.1, AC-2.5): On a compacted fixture with one degraded entry and one gap → report matches the stored arrangement exactly: subjects, forms used, degraded flags, gap reasons, band token counts, config, provenance.\\\\n- **TC-2.2** (AC-2.2, AC-2.3): On a boundary-advanced fixture → tail cost counts short forms short; `loadCost.total` equals the token measure of an actual `pull`'s messages using the same estimator.\\\\n- **TC-2.3** (AC-2.4): Never-compacted thread → view null, tail spans the record, cost-parity assertion holds.\\\\n\\\\n## Flow 3: Message Listing and Viewing\\\\n\\\\nThe drill-down floor. Every report names subjects; this flow is where an operator or agent reads the actual record. Epic 01 shipped `listMessages` bare; this flow completes it and adds the single-message view.\\\\n\\\\n#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-3.1**: Listing returns messages in record order with kind, block summary, token estimate, turn membership, and deleted status, with bounded-listing options (range/limit) so large threads list without loading everything.\\\\n- **AC-3.2**: `messages.show` returns one message in full: every block with complete content (the record — full tool results, not view-shortened forms), token estimate, turn membership, and the message's derivation forms with their states and metadata (joined from the owner's report, including tool-outcome metadata where present).\\\\n- **AC-3.3**: Deleted messages are excluded by default and listable with an explicit include-deleted option, marked deleted — never silently mixed in. `show` on a deleted message returns the record marked deleted (audit is the point), never a not-found.\\\\n- **AC-3.4**: CLI parity: `lhc messages list` and `lhc messages show` mirror the SDK operations — same options, same result JSON.\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Conditions\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-3.1** (AC-3.1): List on the fixture → record order, kinds, token estimates, turn ids correct; range and limit options honored exactly.\\\\n- **TC-3.2** (AC-3.2): Show on a drained tool-result message → full original content present, forms listed with states, outcome metadata present.\\\\n- **TC-3.3** (AC-3.3): Delete one message → default list excludes it; include-deleted lists it marked; show on its id → record with deleted flag.\\\\n- **TC-3.4** (AC-3.4): Spawned-CLI list and show on a fixture thread → JSON equals the in-process SDK results (process suite).\\\\n\\\\n## Flow 4: Derivation Health and Rebuild Visibility\\\\n\\\\nThe state of every derived form, aggregated to act on. This is also where a mutation's rebuild is watched: cleared forms show pending with queued work, then land ready.\\\\n\\\\n#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-4.1**: `inspect.health` aggregates across owners — counts by owner, form kind, and state (ready, pending, retrying, failed, blocked) — assembled entirely from the owners' report surfaces, never from direct `derived_form` or `work_item` reads.\\\\n- **AC-4.2**: Failures carry actionable detail: subject id, form kind, reason, attempts, last error — enough to decide and target a requeue without raw SQL.\\\\n- **AC-4.3**: The report previews repair: which forms a requeue pass would touch (failed and not blocked), reported and never executed.\\\\n- **AC-4.4**: Rebuild visibility: after an edit or delete, health shows the cascade-cleared forms as pending with their queued work visible; after the queue drains, the same forms report ready. Two reads bracket a rebuild.\\\\n- **AC-4.5**: Live queue visibility: `health.queue` reports queued and claimed counts **per form-report entry**, tallied from each entry's live queue-item join in the owners' reports — every pending/retrying form rides one live queue item, so `queued + claimed` equals `pending + retrying` in the same report by construction. These are per-entry counts, not raw `listQueuedWork` work-item counts: one `turn_derivation` work item can back multiple form entries, so a raw work-item count would break that identity.\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Conditions\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-4.1** (AC-4.1, AC-4.5): Fixture with manufactured mixed states (ready, failed-transient, failed-permanent, blocked, pending) → exact counts per owner, kind, and state; queue section consistent with pending counts.\\\\n- **TC-4.2** (AC-4.2, AC-4.3): Failed and blocked forms present → failure detail exact (subject, form, reason, attempts); repair preview lists exactly the failed-not-blocked set.\\\\n- **TC-4.3** (AC-4.4): Edit a mid-thread message → health shows the cascade's cleared set pending with queued work (exact subjects per the cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; nothing outside the cascade changed state.\\\\n\\\\n## Flow 5: Full-Surface Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n\\\\nNot a capstone — nothing here proves integration readiness, because no real inference exists yet (that gate belongs to the inference epic). This is the cross-epic seam proof: the first sequence that drives every surface the PI extension will call, in its call order, against one SDK instance. What it catches: contract drift between the three built epics' surfaces, lifecycle ordering bugs, state leaks between operations.\\\\n\\\\nThe sequence (PI-extension call order): create thread → intake multi-turn tool-heavy batches → background drain settles → status → compact (profile) → pull → inspect (overview, view, health) → edit + delete → rebuild drains → health confirms → second compact → pull → materialize.\\\\n\\\\n#### Acceptance Criteria\\\\n\\\\n- **AC-5.1**: The full sequence completes through one real SDK configuration with the deterministic provider: every operation returns ok, zero network, zero real-provider calls.\\\\n- **AC-5.2**: Checkpoint coherence: post-compact pull serves bands + tail; post-mutation health shows the cleared set pending; post-drain health shows it ready; the second compact's view reflects post-edit content; the second compact receipt's sweep section agrees with the health report taken immediately before it.\\\\n- **AC-5.3**: End-to-end determinism: the whole sequence replayed on a fresh thread produces literally byte-identical pull outputs (they carry no thread id, so equality is asserted with no normalization), and a materialized file byte-identical after normalizing only the intentionally random thread id — the two runs' thread ids are asserted to differ and every other byte must be exact (Story 4 ruling-011).\\\\n- **AC-5.4**: No in-memory dependency: tearing down the SDK instance between phases and continuing on a fresh `createSdk` yields the same end state as the uninterrupted run.\\\\n- **AC-5.5**: Operator parity: inspect and view reads driven through the spawned CLI at checkpoints return the same JSON as the in-process SDK calls at those checkpoints.\\\\n\\\\n#### Test Conditions\\\\n\\\\n- **TC-5.1** (AC-5.1, AC-5.2): Scripted lifecycle with checkpoint assertions at each named step; receipt-vs-health cross-check exact.\\\\n- **TC-5.2** (AC-5.3): Replay on a fresh thread → literal hash equality on every pull output; materialized-file hash equality after substituting only the random thread id, asserting the two thread ids differ and every other byte is exact.\\\\n- **TC-5.3** (AC-5.4): Teardown and recreate the SDK between intake/compact/mutation phases → final pull and health identical to TC-5.1's, and the materialized file hash-equal after substituting only the random thread id (every other byte exact).\\\\n- **TC-5.4** (AC-5.5): Process-suite leg: spawned CLI inspect/view/messages reads at three checkpoints equal the in-process results.\\\\n\\\\n## Data Contracts\\\\n\\\\nContract-level shapes; field mechanics are tech design's. All operations `Promise<OpResult<...>>` taking `ThreadRef`; all read-only.\\\\n\\\\n**`InspectOverview`**: thread (id, createdAt, metadata); events (count, span); messages (visible count, byKind, deletedCount, visibleTokens); turns (open, closed); chunks (count, unchunkedTurns); derivation (counts by state); view (summary | null); visibility (boundaryPosition, zoneTokens).\\\\n\\\\n**`ViewContentsReport`**: meta (viewId, createdAt, profile, config, compactPoint, coveredFrom) | null; bands — ordered entries (subjectKind, subjectId, formUsed, degraded) and stored tokens per band; gaps (band, subjectId, reason); tail (messageCount, tokens as served); loadCost (bandTokens, tailTokens, total — equals what pull serves); sourceState (provenance as stored).\\\\n\\\\n**`threadView.describe`**: the stored active view row exposed read-only — arrangement, gaps, config, source state, identity/timestamps. Absent view → ok with null (not an error). This is the one surface addition outside inspect; it exists so inspect never touches `thread_view` tables.\\\\n\\\\n**`HealthReport`**: owners[] (owner, kind, counts by state); failures[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form, reason, attempts, lastError?); repairPreview[] (owner, subjectKind, subjectId, form); queue (queued, claimed).\\\\n\\\\n**`MessageDetail`** (show): the full `MessageRecord` (all blocks, full content, token estimate, turnId, deleted flag) plus forms: the owner's report entries for this message.\\\\n\\\\n**List options**: bounded listing (range/limit) and includeDeleted; exact option names are tech design's, the *existence* of bounds and the deleted default are contract.\\\\n\\\\n**CLI**: `lhc inspect overview|view|health`, `lhc messages list [--include-deleted] [bounds]`, `lhc messages show --message-id <id>` — JSON to stdout, SDK-parity, same error classes as every epic (`caller_error`, `state_corruption`, `system_error`).\\\\n\\\\n## Non-Functional Requirements\\\\n\\\\n- **Read-only, structurally**: no inspect operation writes — no work rows, no state transitions, no boundary movement. Asserted, not assumed.\\\\n- **No inference in this epic**: no Epic 04 operation invokes a provider; tests may use Epic 02 deterministic-provider setup (draining queued work through the fake) to prepare the derived states under test.\\\\n- **Local and fast**: reports compose domain-surface reads over one thread file; no network, no scans proportional to anything but the thread.\\\\n- **Consistency with served reality**: where a report describes another surface's output (loadCost vs pull), equality is contractual and tested, not aspirational.\\\\n\\\\n## Tech Design Questions\\\\n\\\\n1. `messages.show` shape: new operation vs `listMessages` option — and whether the forms join reuses `messages.report(messageId)` internally or a shared internal read.\\\\n2. `threadView.describe` mapping: stored row → report shape, and whether `describe` and `inspect.view` share assembly code with `status` (they read overlapping state).\\\\n3. `loadCost` mechanism: measure by internally invoking `pull` vs summing the same sources pull reads — equality is the contract either way; pick for cost and locality.\\\\n4. Health assembly: per-owner report calls composed in inspect vs a shared internal join — must stay on surfaces either way.\\\\n5. Lifecycle exercise placement: which legs run in the default suite (TC-5.1 likely) vs the process suite (TC-5.2/5.3/5.4), and where the scripted sequence lives so both legs share it.\\\\n6. Listing bounds: offset/limit vs event-order range — pick from CLI ergonomics; both bounded.\\\\n\\\\n## Story Breakdown\\\\n\\\\nNo Story 0, decided not defaulted: Story-0s exist to land shared substrate that multiple stories would otherwise each half-build — migrations, new tables, config plumbing, fixture families (Epics 01–03 each had at least one of these). This epic has none. The foundation work that does exist is single-consumer and lands with its consumer: the `inspect` surface skeleton and report shapes belong to Story 2 (shapes live in `shared/` per house pattern, so Story 3 consumes without redefining), `threadView.describe` belongs to Story 3 (its only caller is `inspect.view`), and the fixture extension for mutation-in-flight states belongs to Story 2 (its first consumer). A foundation story here would own no checkable behavior of its own. Four stories.\\\\n\\\\n### Story 1: Message Read Surface\\\\n\\\\nCompletes Flow 3: listing options, `show` with forms join, deleted-audit option, CLI extension + parity. Depends only on built code (Epics 01–02). ACs: 3.1–3.4. TCs: 3.1–3.4. ~7 tests.\\\\n\\\\n### Story 2: Inspect Domain — Overview and Health\\\\n\\\\nThe `inspect` domain is born: surface skeleton, `overview` and `health` composed from owners' reports, CLI commands, fixture extension for mutation-in-flight states. Flows 1 and 4. ACs: 1.1–1.4, 4.1–4.5. TCs: 1.1–1.3, 4.1–4.3. ~9 tests.\\\\n\\\\n### Story 3: View-Contents Report\\\\n\\\\n`threadView.describe` (read-only surface addition) + `inspect.view` with the loadCost-equals-pull contract. Flow 2. Depends on Epic 03 Stories 0–2 landed (view storage exists). ACs: 2.1–2.5. TCs: 2.1–2.3. ~6 tests.\\\\n\\\\n### Story 4: Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n\\\\nThe scripted full-surface sequence with checkpoint, replay, teardown, and CLI-parity legs. Flow 5. Depends on Stories 1–3 here plus Epic 03 complete. ACs: 5.1–5.5. TCs: 5.1–5.4. ~6 tests.\\\\n\\\\n**Sequencing**: Story 1 can start immediately (no Epic 03 dependency). Story 2 next (fixture states; health consumes built reports). Story 3 waits on Epic 03's view storage stories. Story 4 last. If Epic 03's build slips, Stories 1–2 proceed; 3–4 wait.\\\\n\\\\n## Traceability\\\\n\\\\n| PRD | This epic |\\\\n|-----|-----------|\\\\n| AC-4.1 (view contents and cost) | Flow 2 |\\\\n| AC-4.2 (messages listable/viewable) | Flow 3 |\\\\n| PRD AC-4.3 (search) | **Deferred post-v1** — Out of Scope; PRD and tech arch already backfilled |\\\\n| AC-4.4 (rebuild visibility) | Flow 4 (AC-4.4) |\\\\n| AC-4.5 (derivation health) | Flow 4 (AC-4.1–4.3, 4.5) |\\\\n| Feature 4 scope: \\\\\\\"thread size and composition, turn and chunk counts\\\\\\\" | Flow 1 |\\\\n| M4 \\\\\\\"SDK exercised end-to-end at its integration points\\\\\\\" | Flow 5 (mechanical half; quality half transfers to the inference epic) |\\\\n\\\\n### AC → TC Table\\\\n\\\\n| AC | TCs |\\\\n|----|-----|\\\\n| AC-1.1 | TC-1.1 |\\\\n| AC-1.2 | TC-1.2 |\\\\n| AC-1.3 | TC-1.1 |\\\\n| AC-1.4 | TC-1.3 |\\\\n| AC-2.1 | TC-2.1 |\\\\n| AC-2.2 | TC-2.2 |\\\\n| AC-2.3 | TC-2.2 |\\\\n| AC-2.4 | TC-2.3 |\\\\n| AC-2.5 | TC-2.1 |\\\\n| AC-3.1 | TC-3.1 |\\\\n| AC-3.2 | TC-3.2 |\\\\n| AC-3.3 | TC-3.3 |\\\\n| AC-3.4 | TC-3.4 |\\\\n| AC-4.1 | TC-4.1 |\\\\n| AC-4.2 | TC-4.2 |\\\\n| AC-4.3 | TC-4.2 |\\\\n| AC-4.4 | TC-4.3 |\\\\n| AC-4.5 | TC-4.1 |\\\\n| AC-5.1 | TC-5.1 |\\\\n| AC-5.2 | TC-5.1 |\\\\n| AC-5.3 | TC-5.2 |\\\\n| AC-5.4 | TC-5.3 |\\\\n| AC-5.5 | TC-5.4 |\\\\n\\\\n## Completeness Self-Check\\\\n\\\\n- [ ] Every PRD Feature 4 AC mapped or explicitly deferred (PRD AC-4.3 search deferred, named, with PRD/tech-arch deferral recorded)\\\\n- [ ] Every flow has ACs and TCs; every AC covered by at least one TC (23/23 per table)\\\\n- [ ] No TC references an undefined AC\\\\n- [ ] Read-only contract stated per flow and as NFR\\\\n- [ ] No new storage, no migration — stated as assumption\\\\n- [ ] Epic 03 in-build dependency named with deviation-table check before tech design freeze\\\\n- [ ] Lifecycle exercise scoped as seam proof, not integration gate; M3/M4 quality-half transfer recorded\\\\n- [ ] No Epic 04 operation invokes inference; provider use only in Epic 02 test setup wording carried\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":266,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":266}}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:82:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CTPnFHx31yUpMPEBAZGK4m\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"code\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Provider output was invalid for claude-code.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"detail\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Provider stdout was not exact JSON.; raw stdout bytes=1075808; raw stdout preview=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"subtype\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"init\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cwd\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"48f0488f-987d-49fe-9ed6-d5d9068f93c3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AskUserQuestion\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bash\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronCreate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronDelete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronList\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DesignSync\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Edit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EnterPlanMode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EnterWorktree\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ExitPlanMode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ExitWorktree\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Monitor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"NotebookEdit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PushNotification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RemoteTrigger\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ScheduleWakeup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Skill\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskCreate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskGet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskList\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskOutput\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskStop\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskUpdate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ToolSearch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"WebFetch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"WebSe...[truncated]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; stdout log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/streams/001-fix-result.stdout.log; stderr log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/streams/001-fix-result.stderr.log\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"artifacts\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"result-envelope\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/001-fix-result.json\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"startedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:55:25.009Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finishedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T16:02:41.059Z\\\\\\\"}\\\\n2\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"b02a2b60-b4b1-44b0-b4a8-2a5d5ee2b2a3\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:04:16.999Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/001-fix-result.json\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"{\\\\\\\"command\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"epic-fix\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"version\\\\\\\":1,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"outcome\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"errors\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"code\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"PROVIDER_OUTPUT_INVALID\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Provider output was invalid for claude-code.\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"detail\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"Provider stdout was not exact JSON.; raw stdout bytes=1075808; raw stdout preview=\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"{\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"system\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"subtype\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"init\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"cwd\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"session_id\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"48f0488f-987d-49fe-9ed6-d5d9068f93c3\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"tools\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\":[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Task\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"AskUserQuestion\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Bash\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronCreate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronDelete\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"CronList\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"DesignSync\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Edit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EnterPlanMode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"EnterWorktree\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ExitPlanMode\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ExitWorktree\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Monitor\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"NotebookEdit\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"PushNotification\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Read\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"RemoteTrigger\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ScheduleWakeup\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Skill\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskCreate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskGet\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskList\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskOutput\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskStop\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"TaskUpdate\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ToolSearch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"WebFetch\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"WebSe...[truncated]\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"; stdout log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/streams/001-fix-result.stdout.log; stderr log=/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/streams/001-fix-result.stderr.log\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"warnings\\\\\\\":[],\\\\\\\"artifacts\\\\\\\":[{\\\\\\\"kind\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"result-envelope\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"path\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/artifacts/fix/001-fix-result.json\\\\\\\"}],\\\\\\\"startedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T15:55:25.009Z\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"finishedAt\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"2026-06-12T16:02:41.059Z\\\\\\\"}\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":2,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":2}}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:122:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01J9mDoFSXXuyHqTdnZd3Vnj\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\\\\n2\\\\t\\\\n3\\\\t**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\\\\n4\\\\t**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\\\\n5\\\\t\\\\n6\\\\t## Context\\\\n7\\\\t\\\\n8\\\\tThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\\\\n9\\\\t\\\\n10\\\\tThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\\\\n11\\\\t\\\\n12\\\\t## Spec Validation\\\\n13\\\\t\\\\n14\\\\tDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\\\\n15\\\\t\\\\n16\\\\t| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\\\\n17\\\\t|---|-------|-----------|--------|\\\\n18\\\\t| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\\\\n19\\\\t| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\\\\n20\\\\t| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\\\\n21\\\\t| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\\\\n22\\\\t| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\\\\\\\"TC-5.1 likely default\\\\\\\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\\\\n23\\\\t\\\\n24\\\\t## System View\\\\n25\\\\t\\\\n26\\\\t```\\\\n27\\\\t                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\\\\n28\\\\t                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\\\\n29\\\\t                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\\\\n30\\\\t                        │     │         │  │           │\\\\n31\\\\t        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\\\\n32\\\\t        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\\\\n33\\\\t   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\\\\n34\\\\t   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\\\\n35\\\\t                                       .pull\\\\n36\\\\t                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\\\\n37\\\\t                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\\\\n38\\\\t```\\\\n39\\\\t\\\\n40\\\\t`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\\\\n41\\\\t\\\\n42\\\\t### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\\\\n43\\\\t\\\\n44\\\\t| Contract | Source | Used by |\\\\n45\\\\t|----------|--------|---------|\\\\n46\\\\t| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\\\\n47\\\\t| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\\\\n48\\\\t| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\\\\n49\\\\t| `listTurns` / `listChunks` | turns (E01) | overview (turn/chunk counts) |\\\\n50\\\\t| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\\\\n51\\\\t| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\\\\n52\\\\t| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\\\\n53\\\\t\\\\n54\\\\t## Module Boundaries\\\\n55\\\\t\\\\n56\\\\t### Placement\\\\n57\\\\t\\\\n58\\\\t```\\\\n59\\\\tsrc/\\\\n60\\\\t  domains/\\\\n61\\\\t    inspect/\\\\n62\\\\t      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\\\\n63\\\\t      internal/\\\\n64\\\\t        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\\\\n65\\\\t        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\\\\n66\\\\t        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\\\\n67\\\\t    thread-view/\\\\n68\\\\t      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\\\\n69\\\\t    messages/\\\\n70\\\\t      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\\\\n71\\\\t  shared/\\\\n72\\\\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\\\\n73\\\\t  cli/\\\\n74\\\\t    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\\\\n75\\\\t    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\\\n76\\\\t  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\\\\n77\\\\t```\\\\n78\\\\t\\\\n79\\\\t### Module Responsibility Matrix\\\\n80\\\\t\\\\n81\\\\t| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\\\\n82\\\\t|--------|------|--------------|\\\\n83\\\\t| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\\\\n84\\\\t| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\\\\n85\\\\t| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\\\\n86\\\\t| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\\\\n87\\\\t| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\\\\n88\\\\t\\\\n89\\\\tDesign decisions:\\\\n90\\\\t\\\\n91\\\\t- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\\\\n92\\\\t- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\\\\n93\\\\t- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\\\\n94\\\\t- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, per-band stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = estimator over pull's served band messages; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for **both** bands and tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented. The per-band stored token counts from `describe` are still reported verbatim in the band section per AC-2.1 (`storedTokens`); they price snapshot bytes and are deliberately not the served `loadCost`, because stored counts omit the served `[context · <band>]` marker headers and tokenization is non-additive (Story 3 ruling-011).\\\\n95\\\\t- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\\\\n96\\\\t- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\\\\n97\\\\t- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\\\\n98\\\\t- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\\\\n99\\\\t\\\\n100\\\\t## Storage\\\\n101\\\\t\\\\n102\\\\tNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\\\\n103\\\\t\\\\n104\\\\t## Flow-by-Flow Design\\\\n105\\\\t\\\\n106\\\\t### Flow 1: Overview\\\\n107\\\\t\\\\n108\\\\t`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\\\\n109\\\\t\\\\n110\\\\tWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\\\\n111\\\\t\\\\n112\\\\t```json\\\\n113\\\\t{\\\\n114\\\\t  \\\\\\\"thread\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"th_…\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"createdAt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\" },\\\\n115\\\\t  \\\\\\\"events\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"count\\\\\\\": 412, \\\\\\\"span\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"first\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"last\\\\\\\": 412 } },\\\\n116\\\\t  \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"visible\\\\\\\": 187, \\\\\\\"byKind\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\": 14, \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\": 41, \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\": 66, \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\": 64, \\\\\\\"assistant_thinking\\\\\\\": 2 }, \\\\\\\"deleted\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"visibleTokens\\\\\\\": 96342 },\\\\n117\\\\t  \\\\\\\"turns\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\": 14 },\\\\n118\\\\t  \\\\\\\"chunks\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"count\\\\\\\": 4, \\\\\\\"unchunkedTurns\\\\\\\": 2 },\\\\n119\\\\t  \\\\\\\"derivation\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\": 118, \\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\": 3, \\\\\\\"retrying\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\": 0 },\\\\n120\\\\t  \\\\\\\"view\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"viewId\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v391\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"createdAt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"compactPoint\\\\\\\": 391, \\\\\\\"coveredFrom\\\\\\\": 12 },\\\\n121\\\\t  \\\\\\\"visibility\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"boundaryPosition\\\\\\\": 398, \\\\\\\"zoneTokens\\\\\\\": 18204 }\\\\n122\\\\t}\\\\n123\\\\t```\\\\n124\\\\t\\\\n125\\\\t### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\\\n126\\\\t\\\\n127\\\\t```\\\\n128\\\\tinspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\\\n129\\\\t      │\\\\n130\\\\t      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\\\n131\\\\t                      │\\\\n132\\\\t                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\\\n133\\\\t                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\\\n134\\\\tloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\\\n135\\\\t```\\\\n136\\\\t\\\\n137\\\\tNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\\\\\"not recomputed\\\\\\\" is structural).\\\\n138\\\\t\\\\n139\\\\t### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\\\n140\\\\t\\\\n141\\\\t`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\\\n142\\\\t\\\\n143\\\\t### Flow 4: Health\\\\n144\\\\t\\\\n145\\\\t`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included), both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts tallied **per form-report entry** from each `FormReportEntry`'s live queue-item join (the entry's `queue` field), so `queued + claimed` equals the same report's `pending + retrying` by construction (AC-4.5, ratified — Epic 04 fix-batch-001). This is deliberately *not* a raw `listQueuedWork` work-item count: one `turn_derivation` work item can back multiple form entries, which would break that identity. Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\\\n146\\\\t\\\\n147\\\\t### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n148\\\\t\\\\n149\\\\tScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\\\n150\\\\t\\\\n151\\\\t## Interface Definitions\\\\n152\\\\t\\\\n153\\\\t`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\\\n154\\\\t\\\\n155\\\\t```typescript\\\\n156\\\\texport interface InspectOverview {\\\\n157\\\\t  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\\\n158\\\\t  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\\\n159\\\\t  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\\\n160\\\\t  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\\\n161\\\\t  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\\\n162\\\\t  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\\\n163\\\\t  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\\\n164\\\\t  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\\\n165\\\\t}\\\\n166\\\\t\\\\n167\\\\texport interface ViewContentsReport {\\\\n168\\\\t  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\\\n169\\\\t          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\\\n170\\\\t          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\\\n171\\\\t  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\\\\\"chunk\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"turn\\\\\\\"; subjectId: string;\\\\n172\\\\t          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\\\n173\\\\t  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\\\n174\\\\t  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\\\n175\\\\t  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\\\n176\\\\t  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\\\n177\\\\t}\\\\n178\\\\t\\\\n179\\\\texport interface HealthReport {\\\\n180\\\\t  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"turns\\\\\\\"; kind: string;\\\\n181\\\\t          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\\\n182\\\\t  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\\\n183\\\\t          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\\\n184\\\\t  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\\\n185\\\\t  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\\\n186\\\\t}\\\\n187\\\\t```\\\\n188\\\\t\\\\n189\\\\tSurface signatures:\\\\n190\\\\t\\\\n191\\\\t```typescript\\\\n192\\\\t// inspect\\\\n193\\\\toverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\\\n194\\\\tview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\\\n195\\\\thealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\\\n196\\\\t// thread-view addition\\\\n197\\\\tdescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\\\n198\\\\t// messages additions\\\\n199\\\\tlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\\\n200\\\\tshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\\\n201\\\\t```\\\\n202\\\\t\\\\n203\\\\tCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\\\n204\\\\t\\\\n205\\\\t```\\\\n206\\\\tlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\\\n207\\\\tlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\\\n208\\\\tlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\\\n209\\\\tlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\\\n210\\\\tlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\\\n211\\\\t```\\\\n212\\\\t\\\\n213\\\\tError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\\\n214\\\\t\\\\n215\\\\t## Testing Strategy\\\\n216\\\\t\\\\n217\\\\tInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\\\\n218\\\\t\\\\n219\\\\t## Work Breakdown\\\\n220\\\\t\\\\n221\\\\tStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\\\\n222\\\\t\\\\n223\\\\t| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\\\\n224\\\\t|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\\\\n225\\\\t| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\\\\n226\\\\t| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\\\\n227\\\\t| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\\\\n228\\\\t| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\\\\n229\\\\t\\\\n230\\\\tSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\\\\n231\\\\t\\\\n232\\\\t## Open Questions\\\\n233\\\\t\\\\n234\\\\tNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\\\\n235\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"b10ee55c-106d-4bd1-9843-047143fbc3b1\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:04:33.961Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/tech-design.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Tech Design\\\\n\\\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech arch:** `../01-tech-arch.md` · **Test plan:** `test-plan.md`\\\\n**Inherits:** Epic 01–03 technical world — storage/transaction rules, error model, `OpResult`, verification tiers, process-suite accounting, CLI conventions. Nothing re-stated here that those designs pin; this document covers what Epic 04 adds.\\\\n\\\\n## Context\\\\n\\\\nThe last epic of the v1 PRD, and the smallest: no migration, no new tables, no derivations, no provider use, no new algorithms. Four read surfaces and a lifecycle exercise. The design problem is not mechanism — it is *composition discipline*: every report assembles other domains' surfaces without touching their tables, and where a report describes another surface's output (`loadCost` vs `pull`), the design makes agreement structural rather than tested-into-existence (the materialize parity-by-construction pattern, reused).\\\\n\\\\nThe second design problem is the dependency posture: this epic consumes Epic 03's surfaces, which finished building days before this design. The epic's handoff gate requires the deviation check below.\\\\n\\\\n## Spec Validation\\\\n\\\\nDesigned from the epic; issues found and resolved during design:\\\\n\\\\n| # | Issue | Resolution | Status |\\\\n|---|-------|-----------|--------|\\\\n| 1 | **Handoff gate (epic Assumptions):** Epic 02/03 final deviation tables vs the contracts this epic consumes | Reviewed all recorded deviations (Epic 02 impl log; Epic 03 impl log: `ViewProfileOverride[]` config typing, `view_boundary` strftime seed, `ViewCompactParams` nested partial, additive error codes, sweep-absent literal superseded by Story 3). None alter consumed shapes: `ViewStatus`, `PullResult`, `thread_view`/`thread_view_band`/`view_boundary` DDL, `messages.report`/`turns.report`, `FormReportEntry`, `MessageRecord.forms` all match spec as built. One *favorable* drift: Epic 02's AC-4.7 ruling attached `forms` to message reads (built for this consumer), so Flow 3's join is thinner than the epic assumed | Gate PASSED — recorded here |\\\\n| 2 | AC-1.1 needs counts (events, messages by kind, tokens) that no surface exposes as counts; inspect may not read tables directly; epic sanctions only one surface addition (`describe`) | Overview composes *list* reads (`listEvents`, `listMessages`, `listTurns`, `listChunks`) and counts in inspect. Cost is linear in thread size — acceptable at v1 scale (NFR allows thread-proportional reads). Count-only surface ops are a deferred optimization, not a v1 need | Resolved — composition, no new surfaces |\\\\n| 3 | Epic Data Contracts leave list-option names to tech design | Pinned: `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }` — `from`/`to` are source-event-order bounds (reports name `sourceEventOrder`, so drill-down uses the coordinate the operator already holds), `limit` caps count after bounds | Resolved — DD-3 |\\\\n| 4 | AC-2.3 equality (`loadCost` totals what pull serves) could be a fragile re-implementation of pull's costing | `inspect.view` *invokes* `threadView.pull` through the surface and measures its output — parity by construction; the TC's independent leg runs a second pull in the test and re-measures. Same pattern as Epic 03's materialize | Resolved — DD-4 |\\\\n| 5 | TC-5.x suite placement left open by epic (TD question 5) | TC-5.1–5.3 default suite (in-process, deterministic, fast); TC-5.4 process suite (spawned CLI). The epic's lean (\\\\\\\"TC-5.1 likely default\\\\\\\") extended after checking runtimes: replay + teardown legs spawn nothing | Resolved — DD-8 |\\\\n\\\\n## System View\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n                    ┌─────────────── inspect (NEW) ───────────────┐\\\\n                    │  overview()      view()       health()      │\\\\n                    └───┬─────┬─────────┬──┬───────────┬──────────┘\\\\n                        │     │         │  │           │\\\\n        ┌───────────────┘     │         │  └───────┐   └────────┐\\\\n        ▼                     ▼         ▼          ▼            ▼\\\\n   threads.resolve      intake-stream  thread-view  messages.report\\\\n   listThreads          .listEvents    .describe(NEW) turns.report\\\\n                                       .pull\\\\n                        messages.listMessages(+opts)\\\\n                        messages.show (NEW)          turns.listTurns/listChunks\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n`inspect` sits at the top of the domain graph: pure consumer, imports five surfaces, nothing imports it except `sdk.ts` and `cli/`. No cycles — unlike Epic 03's sanctioned intake→thread-view cycle, this addition is acyclic by construction. `check-boundaries` gains the domain with no exception entries.\\\\n\\\\n### External Contracts (consumed, as built)\\\\n\\\\n| Contract | Source | Used by |\\\\n|----------|--------|---------|\\\\n| `listEvents` → ordered `EventRecord[]` | intake-stream (E01) | overview (count, span) |\\\\n| `listMessages` → `MessageRecord[]` with `forms?` attached | messages (E01 + E02 AC-4.7) | overview, list/show |\\\\n| `report(ref, {messageId?})` → `FormReportEntry[]` (queue join) | messages/turns (E02) | health, show |\\\\n| `listTurns` / `listChunks` | turns (E01) | overview (turn/chunk counts) |\\\\n| `status` → `ViewStatus` | thread-view (E03) | overview (visibility, derivation counts) |\\\\n| `pull` → `PullResult` | thread-view (E03) | view (loadCost by construction) |\\\\n| `thread_view` row + bands (storage, in-domain) | thread-view (E03) | `describe` only |\\\\n\\\\n## Module Boundaries\\\\n\\\\n### Placement\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nsrc/\\\\n  domains/\\\\n    inspect/\\\\n      index.ts          ← NEW surface: overview, view, health\\\\n      internal/\\\\n        overview.ts     ← compose counts from list reads\\\\n        view-report.ts  ← describe + pull → ViewContentsReport\\\\n        health.ts       ← report joins → HealthReport\\\\n    thread-view/\\\\n      index.ts          ← gains describe() (read-only, ~30 lines)\\\\n    messages/\\\\n      index.ts          ← listMessages gains opts; gains show()\\\\n  shared/\\\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: InspectOverview, ViewContentsReport, HealthReport shapes\\\\n  cli/\\\\n    inspect.ts          ← NEW: lhc inspect overview|view|health\\\\n    messages-read.ts    ← NEW: lhc messages list|show (mutations stay in messages-mutate.ts)\\\\n  sdk.ts                ← gains inspect namespace; threadView.describe; messages.show/list opts\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Module Responsibility Matrix\\\\n\\\\n| Module | Owns | Must NOT own |\\\\n|--------|------|--------------|\\\\n| `inspect/index.ts` + internal | Report assembly, counting, shaping | Any table read, any write, any provider call, any derivation interpretation beyond the owners' reported states |\\\\n| `thread-view/describe` | Exposing stored view row (arrangement, gaps, config, source state) | Recomputing anything; mutating; reading the record |\\\\n| `messages/show` | Single-record read (full blocks) + `report(messageId)` composition | View-form shortening (show returns the record — full tool results, never boundary-shortened) |\\\\n| `messages/listMessages` opts | Bounds, limit, deleted filter | Default-including deleted (audit is opt-in) |\\\\n| `cli/inspect.ts`, `cli/messages-read.ts` | argv → SDK → JSON stdout | Any logic beyond arg mapping (CLI parity is structural: same code path as SDK) |\\\\n\\\\nDesign decisions:\\\\n\\\\n- **DD-1 (describe placement):** `describe` lives in thread-view because the stored view row is thread-view's table; inspect consuming it through the surface keeps the must-not-own rule airtight. Absent view → `ok` with `null`, mirroring `status`'s never-compacted behavior.\\\\n- **DD-2 (show composes report):** `show` = internal single-message read (same store read as `listMessages`, by id, full blocks) + `messages.report(ref, {messageId})` for the queue-joined forms. No new join machinery; `FormReportEntry` is the forms shape `show` returns.\\\\n- **DD-3 (list options):** `{ from?, to?, limit?, includeDeleted? }`, bounds in source event order. Existing callers unaffected (opts optional, default behavior unchanged: all visible messages).\\\\n- **DD-4 (loadCost by construction):** `view-report.ts` calls `describe` (stored bands: entries, gaps, config, per-band stored token counts) and `pull` (served messages). `loadCost.bandTokens` = estimator over pull's served band messages; `loadCost.tailTokens` = estimator over pull's tail messages (band-absent entries); `total` = sum. Pull is the single costing authority for **both** bands and tail — AC-2.2's boundary-aware shortening is inherited, not re-implemented. The per-band stored token counts from `describe` are still reported verbatim in the band section per AC-2.1 (`storedTokens`); they price snapshot bytes and are deliberately not the served `loadCost`, because stored counts omit the served `[context · <band>]` marker headers and tokenization is non-additive (Story 3 ruling-011).\\\\n- **DD-5 (overview's view section):** composed from `status` (boundary, zone, derivation counts, view health) + `describe` (viewId, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom) — both already exist; overview adds no view logic.\\\\n- **DD-6 (read-only, structurally tested):** the architecture-risk test snapshots observable state (work-item rows via `listQueuedWork`/reports, boundary position via `status`, view identity via `describe`, event/message counts) before and after every inspect/describe/show/list call and asserts deep equality. Read-only is asserted as absence-of-delta, not absence-of-write-code.\\\\n- **DD-7 (no migration):** schema terminal at v6. The one index temptation (message kind counts) is declined — counts come from list reads (Spec Validation #2); if profiling ever demands an index, that is a v7 proposal.\\\\n- **DD-8 (suite placement):** TC-5.1–5.3 default suite; TC-5.4 process suite. The lifecycle script is a shared fixture helper (`test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`) both suites drive, so the spawned leg replays the same sequence rather than a re-described one.\\\\n\\\\n## Storage\\\\n\\\\nNone. No tables, no migration, no new indexes (DD-7). The only storage *read* this epic adds is `describe`'s in-domain read of `thread_view` / `thread_view_band` / `view_boundary`, all Epic 03 tables.\\\\n\\\\n## Flow-by-Flow Design\\\\n\\\\n### Flow 1: Overview\\\\n\\\\n`overview(ref)`: resolve thread (registry metadata) → `listEvents` (count, first/last order) → `listMessages({includeDeleted: true})` (visible/deleted split, kind counts, visible token sum — deleted detected per the read contract's flag) → `listTurns` (open/closed counts) → `listChunks` (count; unchunked = closed turns minus chunk-member turns) → `status` + `describe` (derivation counts, visibility, view summary). Each piece independent; fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild shapes fall out of the same composition path: absent pieces are zeros/nulls; no shape-specific branch is allowed except normalizing null sections.\\\\n\\\\nWorked example (compacted fixture, abridged):\\\\n\\\\n```json\\\\n{\\\\n  \\\\\\\"thread\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"th_…\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"createdAt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\" },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"events\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"count\\\\\\\": 412, \\\\\\\"span\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"first\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"last\\\\\\\": 412 } },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"visible\\\\\\\": 187, \\\\\\\"byKind\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"user_prompt\\\\\\\": 14, \\\\\\\"assistant_text\\\\\\\": 41, \\\\\\\"tool_call\\\\\\\": 66, \\\\\\\"tool_result\\\\\\\": 64, \\\\\\\"assistant_thinking\\\\\\\": 2 }, \\\\\\\"deleted\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"visibleTokens\\\\\\\": 96342 },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"turns\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\": 0, \\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\": 14 },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"chunks\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"count\\\\\\\": 4, \\\\\\\"unchunkedTurns\\\\\\\": 2 },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"derivation\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"ready\\\\\\\": 118, \\\\\\\"pending\\\\\\\": 3, \\\\\\\"retrying\\\\\\\": 1, \\\\\\\"failed\\\\\\\": 2, \\\\\\\"blocked\\\\\\\": 0 },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"view\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"viewId\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"v391\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"createdAt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"…\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"compactPoint\\\\\\\": 391, \\\\\\\"coveredFrom\\\\\\\": 12 },\\\\n  \\\\\\\"visibility\\\\\\\": { \\\\\\\"boundaryPosition\\\\\\\": 398, \\\\\\\"zoneTokens\\\\\\\": 18204 }\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Flow 2: View Contents Report\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\ninspect.view ──► threadView.describe ──► stored arrangement/gaps/config/band tokens/source state\\\\n      │\\\\n      └────────► threadView.pull ──► served messages\\\\n                      │\\\\n                      ├─ band entries → cross-check count only (arrangement is describe's)\\\\n                      └─ tail entries → estimator → tailTokens (as served: short forms short)\\\\nloadCost = { bandTokens: Σ stored, tailTokens: measured, total: sum }\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nNever-compacted: `describe` → null ⇒ `meta: null`, bands empty, whole pull output is tail, parity contract unchanged (AC-2.4). The report never recomputes selection, rendering, or boundary state — stored snapshot + live pull are the only sources (AC-2.1's \\\\\\\"not recomputed\\\\\\\" is structural).\\\\n\\\\n### Flow 3: Message Listing and Show\\\\n\\\\n`listMessages(ref, opts)`: existing read + WHERE bounds on `source_event_order`, LIMIT, deleted filter (default excluded; `includeDeleted` includes flagged). `show(ref, messageId)`: by-id read, full blocks verbatim from the record, `deleted` flag honest, forms from `report({messageId})`. Not-found → `message_not_found` (existing code). Deleted + show → `ok` with flagged record (AC-3.3: audit, never not-found).\\\\n\\\\n### Flow 4: Health\\\\n\\\\n`health(ref)`: `messages.report` + `turns.report` (full, not-ready included), both owners. Compose: counts by owner/kind/state from report entries' states; `failures[]` from `failed`/`blocked` entries (reason, attempts, lastError off `FormReportEntry`); `repairPreview[]` = failed-and-not-blocked subjects (reported, never requeued — AC-4.3); `queue` = queued/claimed counts tallied **per form-report entry** from each `FormReportEntry`'s live queue-item join (the entry's `queue` field), so `queued + claimed` equals the same report's `pending + retrying` by construction (AC-4.5, ratified — Epic 04 fix-batch-001). This is deliberately *not* a raw `listQueuedWork` work-item count: one `turn_derivation` work item can back multiple form entries, which would break that identity. Rebuild visibility (AC-4.4) is two health calls bracketing a drain — no new mechanism, the cascade's pending states simply show.\\\\n\\\\n### Flow 5: Lifecycle Exercise\\\\n\\\\nScripted in `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts`: phases named `create | intake | drain | status | compact1 | pull1 | inspect1 | mutate | rebuild | health2 | compact2 | pull2 | materialize`. Each phase returns its results to the driving test; checkpoint assertions live in the test, not the script. Teardown leg (TC-5.3) re-creates the SDK between named phase groups using the same script with a `freshSdk` hook. Receipt-vs-health cross-check (AC-5.2): `compact2`'s receipt sweep section against the `health2` snapshot taken immediately before — field-level equality on the failed/requeued sets.\\\\n\\\\n## Interface Definitions\\\\n\\\\n`src/shared/inspect.ts` (load-bearing shapes; field comments carry AC refs in source):\\\\n\\\\n```typescript\\\\nexport interface InspectOverview {\\\\n  thread: { id: string; createdAt: string; metadata?: Record<string, string> };\\\\n  events: { count: number; span: { first: number; last: number } | null };\\\\n  messages: { visible: number; byKind: Record<string, number>; deleted: number; visibleTokens: number };\\\\n  turns: { open: number; closed: number };\\\\n  chunks: { count: number; unchunkedTurns: number };\\\\n  derivation: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number };\\\\n  view: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\\\n  visibility: { boundaryPosition: number; zoneTokens: number };\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface ViewContentsReport {\\\\n  meta: { viewId: string; createdAt: string; profile: string | null;\\\\n          config: { lowerBound: number; percentages: Record<string, number> };\\\\n          compactPoint: number; coveredFrom: number } | null;\\\\n  bands: Array<{ band: Band; entries: Array<{ subjectKind: \\\\\\\"chunk\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"turn\\\\\\\"; subjectId: string;\\\\n          formUsed: string; degraded: boolean }>; storedTokens: number }>;\\\\n  gaps: Array<{ band: Band; subjectId: string; reason: string }>;\\\\n  tail: { messageCount: number; tokens: number };          // as served (AC-2.2)\\\\n  loadCost: { bandTokens: number; tailTokens: number; total: number }; // = pull (AC-2.3)\\\\n  sourceState: { maxEventOrder: number; formCounts: Record<string, number> }; // provenance verbatim (AC-2.5)\\\\n}\\\\n\\\\nexport interface HealthReport {\\\\n  owners: Array<{ owner: \\\\\\\"messages\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"turns\\\\\\\"; kind: string;\\\\n          counts: { ready: number; pending: number; retrying: number; failed: number; blocked: number } }>;\\\\n  failures: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string;\\\\n          reason: string; attempts: number; lastError?: string }>;\\\\n  repairPreview: Array<{ owner: string; subjectKind: string; subjectId: string; form: string }>;\\\\n  queue: { queued: number; claimed: number };\\\\n}\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nSurface signatures:\\\\n\\\\n```typescript\\\\n// inspect\\\\noverview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<InspectOverview>>;\\\\nview(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<ViewContentsReport>>;\\\\nhealth(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<HealthReport>>;\\\\n// thread-view addition\\\\ndescribe(ref: ThreadRef): Promise<OpResult<StoredView | null>>;   // StoredView mirrors the row: id, createdAt, compactPoint, coveredFrom, profileName, config, arrangement, gaps, sourceState, bands (band → storedTokens)\\\\n// messages additions\\\\nlistMessages(ref: ThreadRef, opts?: { from?: number; to?: number; limit?: number; includeDeleted?: boolean }): Promise<OpResult<MessageRecord[]>>;\\\\nshow(ref: ThreadRef, messageId: string): Promise<OpResult<MessageDetail>>;  // MessageRecord (full blocks, deleted flag) + forms: FormReportEntry[]\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nCLI grammar (JSON stdout, existing error classes, exit conventions inherited):\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\nlhc inspect overview --thread <ref>\\\\nlhc inspect view     --thread <ref>\\\\nlhc inspect health   --thread <ref>\\\\nlhc messages list    --thread <ref> [--from <n>] [--to <n>] [--limit <n>] [--include-deleted]\\\\nlhc messages show    --thread <ref> --message-id <id>\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nError codes: no additions. `thread_not_found`, `message_not_found`, `caller_error` (bad bounds: `from > to`, `limit < 1`), `state_corruption`, `system_error` — all existing.\\\\n\\\\n## Testing Strategy\\\\n\\\\nInherited wholesale from Epics 01–03: real temp SQLite, no mocks anywhere but the provider seam (unused here beyond fixture prep), default + process suites, zero-provider assertion extended to all inspect/show/list/describe operations. New emphasis — the **read-only delta assert** (DD-6) is this epic's architecture-risk centerpiece: every new operation runs under a before/after observable-state snapshot in one shared helper. Direct table-read prevention is static: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, and this epic adds a source check that `domains/inspect/**` contains no raw SQL table-name access to other domains' tables. Test files: `inspect-overview.test.ts`, `inspect-view.test.ts`, `messages-read.test.ts`, `inspect-health.test.ts`, `lifecycle.test.ts`, `cli-process-inspect.test.ts` (process suite). Full TC mapping, fixture extensions, and Red/Green detail: `test-plan.md`.\\\\n\\\\n## Work Breakdown\\\\n\\\\nStory chunks follow the epic's four stories; per-chunk Red/Green and counts in the test plan.\\\\n\\\\n| Chunk | Story | Builds | Risk concentration |\\\\n|-------|-------|--------|--------------------|\\\\n| 1 | S1 Message reads | list opts, show, `cli/messages-read.ts` | Bounds semantics; deleted default; show returning record-not-view forms |\\\\n| 2 | S2 Inspect domain | surface + overview + health, `shared/inspect.ts`, `cli/inspect.ts`, fixture mutation-states extension | Count correctness vs fixture ground truth; health composition staying on surfaces |\\\\n| 3 | S3 View report | `describe`, `view-report.ts` | Parity-by-construction wiring; never-compacted nulls |\\\\n| 4 | S4 Lifecycle | `lifecycle.ts` script + 4 TC legs | Checkpoint ordering; receipt-vs-health equality; teardown continuity |\\\\n\\\\nSequencing: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 (3 needs Epic 03 storage live — already landed; 4 needs 1–3).\\\\n\\\\n## Open Questions\\\\n\\\\nNone blocking. Deferred items: count-only surface ops if thread scale ever makes overview's list-composition measurable (Spec Validation #2); message search (post-v1, PRD-recorded).\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":235,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":235}}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:193:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_012GXuneDbCZxRVi3CKrBGxH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"1\\\\t# Epic 04: Inspection — Test Plan\\\\n2\\\\t\\\\n3\\\\t**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\\\\n4\\\\tInherits Epic 01–03 test architecture: real temp SQLite per test, deterministic provider for fixture prep only, default suite (`pnpm verify`) + process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`), suite-accounting row, red manifest discipline.\\\\n5\\\\t\\\\n6\\\\t## Test Files\\\\n7\\\\t\\\\n8\\\\t| File | Suite | Covers |\\\\n9\\\\t|------|-------|--------|\\\\n10\\\\t| `test/messages-read.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.3 + list/show read-only legs |\\\\n11\\\\t| `test/inspect-overview.test.ts` | default | TC-1.1–1.3 |\\\\n12\\\\t| `test/inspect-view.test.ts` | default | TC-2.1–2.3 + describe legs |\\\\n13\\\\t| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\\\\n14\\\\t| `test/lifecycle.test.ts` | default | TC-5.1–5.3 |\\\\n15\\\\t| `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` | process | TC-3.4, TC-5.4 |\\\\n16\\\\t| `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` | (helper) | the scripted sequence both suites drive |\\\\n17\\\\t\\\\n18\\\\tFixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\\\n19\\\\t\\\\n20\\\\t## TC → Test Mapping\\\\n21\\\\t\\\\n22\\\\t| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\\\n23\\\\t|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\\\n24\\\\t| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\\\n25\\\\t| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\\\n26\\\\t| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\\\n27\\\\t| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\\\n28\\\\t| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\\\n29\\\\t| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\\\n30\\\\t| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\\\n31\\\\t| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\\\n32\\\\t| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\\\n33\\\\t| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\\\n34\\\\t| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\\\n35\\\\t| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\\\n36\\\\t| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\\\n37\\\\t| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\\\n38\\\\t| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → literal hash-equal pull outputs; materialized file hash-equal after normalizing only the random thread id (ids asserted to differ, every other byte exact) |\\\\n39\\\\t| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\\\n40\\\\t| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\\\n41\\\\t\\\\n42\\\\t## Architecture-Risk Tests\\\\n43\\\\t\\\\n44\\\\t| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\\\n45\\\\t|------|------|--------------|\\\\n46\\\\t| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\\\\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\\\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\\\n47\\\\t| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\\\n48\\\\t| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\\\n49\\\\t| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\\\n50\\\\t| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\\\n51\\\\t\\\\n52\\\\t## Suite Accounting\\\\n53\\\\t\\\\n54\\\\tDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\\\n55\\\\t\\\\n56\\\\t## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\\\n57\\\\t\\\\n58\\\\t**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\\\n59\\\\t\\\\n60\\\\t**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\\\n61\\\\t\\\\n62\\\\t**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\\\n63\\\\t\\\\n64\\\\t**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\\\n65\\\\t\\\\n66\\\\t## Verification\\\\n67\\\\t\\\\n68\\\\tPer-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\\\\n69\\\\t\\\"}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"22f017d9-78fc-44d0-9063-de9389c2247f\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:05:11.203Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"text\\\",\\\"file\\\":{\\\"filePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/04-inspection/test-plan.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Epic 04: Inspection — Test Plan\\\\n\\\\n**Epic:** `epic.md` (23 ACs / 17 TCs) · **Tech design:** `tech-design.md`\\\\nInherits Epic 01–03 test architecture: real temp SQLite per test, deterministic provider for fixture prep only, default suite (`pnpm verify`) + process suite (`LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all`), suite-accounting row, red manifest discipline.\\\\n\\\\n## Test Files\\\\n\\\\n| File | Suite | Covers |\\\\n|------|-------|--------|\\\\n| `test/messages-read.test.ts` | default | TC-3.1–3.3 + list/show read-only legs |\\\\n| `test/inspect-overview.test.ts` | default | TC-1.1–1.3 |\\\\n| `test/inspect-view.test.ts` | default | TC-2.1–2.3 + describe legs |\\\\n| `test/inspect-health.test.ts` | default | TC-4.1–4.3 |\\\\n| `test/lifecycle.test.ts` | default | TC-5.1–5.3 |\\\\n| `test/cli-process-inspect.test.ts` | process | TC-3.4, TC-5.4 |\\\\n| `test/fixtures/lifecycle.ts` | (helper) | the scripted sequence both suites drive |\\\\n\\\\nFixture: Epic 03's tool-heavy fixture reused; extended in place (Story 2) with a mutation-in-flight variant — one edit applied, drain *not* settled, so cleared-pending states are real production states, not hand-written rows (FC-fidelity rule carried from Epic 03 Story 0: states reached through intake → mutate → partial drain, never direct `derived_form` writes).\\\\n\\\\n## TC → Test Mapping\\\\n\\\\n| TC | Test (file :: name) | Assertion spine |\\\\n|----|--------------------|-----------------|\\\\n| TC-1.1 | inspect-overview :: full shape variants | fresh-empty, mid-first-turn, never-compacted-with-record, compacted, and mid-rebuild all return the full shape with absent pieces as zeros/nulls; compacted fixture exact counts per section vs fixture ground truth |\\\\n| TC-1.2 | inspect-overview :: deleted accounting | delete one → visible−1, deleted=1, kind map excludes, tokens drop by its estimate, event count unchanged |\\\\n| TC-1.3 | inspect-overview :: purity | two calls, no writes between → deep-equal; read-only delta assert green; zero provider calls |\\\\n| TC-2.1 | inspect-view :: arrangement fidelity | entries/forms/degraded/gap reasons/config/provenance equal `describe` output equal stored row (degraded + gap fixture) |\\\\n| TC-2.2 | inspect-view :: loadCost parity on boundary-advanced fixture | tail costs short forms short; `total` = estimator over an independent `pull`'s messages |\\\\n| TC-2.3 | inspect-view :: never-compacted | `meta: null`, bands `[]`, tail spans record, parity holds |\\\\n| TC-3.1 | messages-read :: order, fields, bounds | record order; kind/tokens/turnId present; `from`/`to`/`limit` exact windows; `from > to` → `caller_error` |\\\\n| TC-3.2 | messages-read :: show full record + forms | drained tool-result: full content (not shortened), forms with states, outcome metadata present |\\\\n| TC-3.3 | messages-read :: deleted handling | default list excludes; `includeDeleted` marks; show on deleted → ok + flag; show on missing id → `message_not_found` |\\\\n| TC-3.4 | cli-process-inspect :: list/show parity | spawned `lhc messages list/show` JSON deep-equals in-process SDK results |\\\\n| TC-4.1 | inspect-health :: counts + queue consistency | mixed-state fixture: exact counts per owner/kind/state; queue section equals live-item counts from the same reports |\\\\n| TC-4.2 | inspect-health :: failure detail + preview | failed: reason/attempts/lastError exact; blocked excluded from preview; preview = failed∧¬blocked set exactly |\\\\n| TC-4.3 | inspect-health :: rebuild bracket | edit → health: cascade set pending with queued work visible (exact subjects per cascade contract); `drainSettled` → same set ready; disjoint forms untouched |\\\\n| TC-5.1 | lifecycle :: full sequence + checkpoints | every phase ok; post-compact pull = bands+tail; mutate → pending; drain → ready; compact2 reflects edit; receipt sweep section field-equals pre-compact health snapshot |\\\\n| TC-5.2 | lifecycle :: replay determinism | fresh thread, same script → literal hash-equal pull outputs; materialized file hash-equal after normalizing only the random thread id (ids asserted to differ, every other byte exact) |\\\\n| TC-5.3 | lifecycle :: teardown continuity | `freshSdk` between phase groups → final pull/health/file identical to TC-5.1 run |\\\\n| TC-5.4 | cli-process-inspect :: checkpoint parity | spawned CLI overview/view/list at three checkpoints deep-equal in-process results at same checkpoints |\\\\n\\\\n## Architecture-Risk Tests\\\\n\\\\n| Risk | Test | Why it bites |\\\\n|------|------|--------------|\\\\n| Inspect quietly writes (work rows, boundary nudge, view touch) | **read-only delta assert**: shared helper snapshots observable state (queued work via owners, boundary/zone via status, view identity via describe, event/message counts) before/after *every* new operation; deep-equal after. Runs inside each TC file via wrapper | A single forgotten side effect makes \\\\\\\"inspect describes, never changes\\\\\\\" fiction; absence-of-delta is checkable, absence-of-write-code is not |\\\\n| Zero-provider on all new ops | suite-wide assert extended: overview/view/health/describe/show/list under a throwing provider config → all ok | The no-inference NFR stays structural through the last epic |\\\\n| `loadCost` drifts from served reality | TC-2.2's independent-pull leg + lifecycle TC-5.1 checkpoint (report at compact1 vs pull1) | Parity by construction can still break at the estimator seam; two independent measurements pin it |\\\\n| Health re-derives instead of composing | health tests assert composition through owner surfaces only: `check-boundaries` forbids cross-domain internal imports, an Epic 04 source check rejects raw SQL references to other domains' tables from `domains/inspect/**`, and the read-only delta assert separately catches writes | The must-not-own rule is the domain's entire contract |\\\\n| Lifecycle order bugs only visible cross-epic | TC-5.1's named-phase checkpoints; receipt-vs-health field equality | First sequence ever to run all surfaces in PI-extension order; seam drift between three separately-built epics surfaces here or in production |\\\\n\\\\n## Suite Accounting\\\\n\\\\nDefault suite grows ~26 tests across 5 files. Process suite grows TC-3.4 + TC-5.4 (2 spawned scenarios, ~6 assertions); accounting row carried: process suite `ran | not-ran` recorded per verify-all invocation, never silently skipped.\\\\n\\\\n## Chunk Red/Green Detail\\\\n\\\\n**Chunk 1 — message reads (S1).** Red: `show` absent from surface (structured not-implemented per house stub rule); list opts ignored — bounds test fails on full-list return. Green: opts → WHERE/LIMIT; show + report join; `cli/messages-read.ts`; TC-3.1–3.3 + read-only legs. ~8 tests.\\\\n\\\\n**Chunk 2 — inspect domain (S2).** Red: `inspect.*` stubs return not-implemented; fixture lacks mutation-variant (TC-4.3 unwritable → fixture work first). Green: `shared/inspect.ts` shapes; overview composition; health composition; `cli/inspect.ts`; delta-assert helper lands here and wraps Chunk 1's ops retroactively. TC-1.1–1.3, TC-4.1–4.3. ~11 tests.\\\\n\\\\n**Chunk 3 — view report (S3).** Red: `describe` absent; `inspect.view` stub. Green: `describe` (row → `StoredView`), `view-report.ts` (describe + pull → report), TC-2.1–2.3 + describe null/shape legs. ~6 tests.\\\\n\\\\n**Chunk 4 — lifecycle (S4).** Red: `lifecycle.ts` helper absent; all four TC files reference it. Green: script with named phases + `freshSdk` hook; TC-5.1–5.3 default; TC-5.4 process. ~7 tests (4 scenarios, multi-checkpoint).\\\\n\\\\n## Verification\\\\n\\\\nPer-story: `pnpm verify` (lint, typecheck, default suites). Story 4 and epic close: `LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1 pnpm verify-all` — process suite must report `ran`. Red manifests regenerated per chunk per house discipline; no Epic 01–03 test amendments expected (additive surfaces only — list-opts default behavior is unchanged, existing `listMessages` callers see identical results).\\\\n\\\",\\\"numLines\\\":69,\\\"startLine\\\":1,\\\"totalLines\\\":69}}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/04-inspection/artifacts/epic/streams/002-epic-reverify.stdout.log:246:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01ELwkEHjWMw99tDtrspywG6\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"119:#### Spec Deviations\\\\n120-\\\\n121-**Ruling-011** (`03-view-contents-report-story-run-001-ruling-011`) — decision: *approve measured `bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState` as accepted deviations* (the accepted public contract for `inspect.view`).\\\\n122-\\\\n123-- **Measured `loadCost.bandTokens` (AC-2.1 / AC-2.3).** AC-2.3 is the governing contract: `loadCost.total` must equal what an actual `pull` serves, verified against an independent pull. Stored band `token_count` prices snapshot bytes without the served `[context · <band>]` marker headers, and tokenization is non-additive, so a stored-count sum can never satisfy that equality. `bandTokens` is therefore measured over pull's served band messages with the shared estimator. AC-2.1's per-band stored token counts remain reported verbatim from the stored snapshot in the band section (`storedTokens`).\\\\n124-- **Nullable `sourceState` (AC-2.4 / AC-2.5).** A never-compacted thread has no recorded compact provenance; AC-2.5 requires recorded provenance verbatim, so `sourceState` is `null` for such threads (mirroring AC-2.4's `meta: null`) rather than fabricated zeros.\\\\n125-- **Not a weakening.** Both deviations honor the governing ACs more faithfully than the literal stored-sum / zeros reading would; approved on the merits via ruling-011 and recorded again for the spec-deviation gate.\\\\n126-\\\\n127-### Definition of Done\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"77af4b8d-fd36-430f-8eea-47bd404bad4c\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"d239e304-2bf4-49b4-8a51-84ff7a592e9c\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-06-12T16:05:30.221Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"119:#### Spec Deviations\\\\n120-\\\\n121-**Ruling-011** (`03-view-contents-report-story-run-001-ruling-011`) — decision: *approve measured `bandTokens` and nullable `sourceState` as accepted deviations* (the accepted public contract for `inspect.view`).\\\\n122-\\\\n123-- **Measured `loadCost.bandTokens` (AC-2.1 / AC-2.3).** AC-2.3 is the governing contract: `loadCost.total` must equal what an actual `pull` serves, verified against an independent pull. Stored band `token_count` prices snapshot bytes without the served `[context · <band>]` marker headers, and tokenization is non-additive, so a stored-count sum can never satisfy that equality. `bandTokens` is therefore measured over pull's served band messages with the shared estimator. AC-2.1's per-band stored token counts remain reported verbatim from the stored snapshot in the band section (`storedTokens`).\\\\n124-- **Nullable `sourceState` (AC-2.4 / AC-2.5).** A never-compacted thread has no recorded compact provenance; AC-2.5 requires recorded provenance verbatim, so `sourceState` is `null` for such threads (mirroring AC-2.4's `meta: null`) rather than fabricated zeros.\\\\n125-- **Not a weakening.** Both deviations honor the governing ACs more faithfully than the literal stored-sum / zeros reading would; approved on the merits via ruling-011 and recorded again for the spec-deviation gate.\\\\n126-\\\\n127-### Definition of Done\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false}}\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/05-derivation-inference/tech-design.md:212:## Interface Definitions\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/05-render-targets.md:112:### Definition of Done\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/stories/05-render-targets.md:113:<!-- Jira: Definition of Done or Acceptance Criteria footer -->\\n./docs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/005-story-orchestrate-resume.json:1:{\\\"command\\\":\\\"story-orchestrate resume\\\",\\\"version\\\":1,\\\"status\\\":\\\"needs-user-decision\\\",\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-ruling\\\",\\\"result\\\":{\\\"case\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-ruling\\\",\\\"storyId\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact\\\",\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact-story-run-001\\\",\\\"currentSnapshotPath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/story-lead/001-current.json\\\",\\\"eventHistoryPath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/story-lead/001-events.jsonl\\\",\\\"finalPackagePath\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/story-lead/001-final-package.json\\\",\\\"finalPackage\\\":{\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-ruling\\\",\\\"storyRunId\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact-story-run-001\\\",\\\"storyId\\\":\\\"02-smart-compact\\\",\\\"attempt\\\":1,\\\"summary\\\":{\\\"storyTitle\\\":\\\"Story 2: Smart Compact\\\",\\\"implementedScope\\\":\\\"Applied impl-lead ruling 02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-013 exactly. SV-02-001 (extra-rule selection behavior): rewrote selectArrangement to the literal Story 2 / tech-design rules 1–6 with the pinned tie-breakers only — one shared fill rule for all three bands (newest-first whole-entry fill, ≤ inclusion, first crossing entry stops the band, included only when the band was still empty so one oversized entry still represents), and chunk candidacy decided literally by the pinned newest-member tie-breaker (newest live member behind the compact point and older than the smooth band's oldest included turn). Removed the smooth-obligate beyond-share inclusion, the partial-chunk retreat, and the brief-band loner suppression — the brief band now uses the same fill rule as rules 2–3, and the coverage edge falls out of it naturally (the loner returns immediately, so chunks remaining after it are excluded and reported via covered_from). Regenerated all committed goldens G1–G4 from the literal rules (verified against the pure walk before committing; README records the ruling-sanctioned regeneration). SV-02-002 (receipt total): added explicit CompactReceipt.totalTokens (band tokens + tail tokens, the assembled actual vs the target bound) and asserted it in TC-2.2 (equals the band/tail sum, lands under the bound on this fixture) and in TC-2.1's receipt coverage (all-tail compact: totalTokens === tailTokens). Sweep remains the literal \\\\\\\"absent\\\\\\\". Updated view-compact.test.ts reference configs to literal-rule arrangements: TARGET_PARAMS (equal shares) for TC-2.2, GRADIENT_PARAMS 25/16/10/49 (all three bands non-empty) for TC-2.6/restart/TC-2.4/TC-1.3/TC-1.5, and a new EDGE_PARAMS (100, 50/10/10/30) whose compact point at t10's close yields three chunk candidates so the brief share holds c2 and genuinely excludes c1 (covered_from 13, no phantom gaps). TC-2.3's degraded-thread config needed no change — the literal walk produces the same degraded/gap arrangement. Both gates rerun green.\\\",\\\"acceptanceRationale\\\":\\\"Story-lead is pausing for caller ruling 02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-spec-deviation before impl-lead can accept the story.\\\"},\\\"evidence\\\":{\\\"implementorArtifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"implementor-result\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/003-implementor.json\\\",\\\"provenance\\\":\\\"current-run\\\"},{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"implementor-result\\\",\\\"path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/03-thread-views-and-smart-compact/artifacts/02-smart-compact/006-continue.json\\\",\\\"provenance\\\":\\\"current-run\\\"}],\\\"selfReviewArtifacts\\\":[],\\\"verifierArtifacts\\\":[{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"verifi